{"abstract":"Aims The recent DanGer shock trial found reduced mortality, but increased risk of acute kidney injury (AKI) in patients treated with a microaxial flow pump after an acute myocardial infarct with cardiogenic shock. AKI has previously been associated with increased short-term mortality, whereas data on long-term outcomes are sparse. We aimed to describe the frequency of AKI and associated risk factors as well as long-term mortality and morbidity. Methods and results A retrospective observational study comprising patients admitted with acute myocardial infarction cardiogenic shock in Denmark between 2010 and 2017 with data on kidney function from the RETROSHOCK cohort. National health registry data enabled 10-year follow-up to assess mortality and morbidity. Kaplan-Meier estimates and competing risks regression were used to evaluate the association of AKI with the incidence of short- and long-term mortality, chronic kidney disease (CKD) and dialysis. Among 1473 patients, 44% developed AKI, 25% required renal replacement therapy (RRT). AKI development was associated with increasing age, diabetes, low ejection fraction and high lactate levels on admission (P < 0.05). Thirty-days mortality as well as mortality at 1-, 5-, and 10-years follow-up was significantly increased in patients with AKI; at 10 years follow-up mortality was increased by more than 30% (P < 0.001). The 10-year cumulative incidence of both CKD and dialysis, accounting for the competing risk of death, was significantly higher in patients treated with RRT during admission (P < 0.001). Conclusion AKI was associated with increased short- and long-term mortality and morbidity, including CKD and dialysis, but not new cardiovascular events.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Bjørn, Maria","Kunkel, Joakim Bo","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Josiassen, Jakob","Jeppesen, Karoline Korsholm","Holmvang, Lene","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Schmidt, Henrik","Fosbøl, Emil","Hassager, Christian","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Ravn, Hanne Berg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-830881"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Bjørn, Maria"],"keyword":["Acute kidney injury","Acute myocardial infarction","Cardiogenic shock","Chronic kidney disease","Intensive care","Renal Replacement Therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term outcomes after acute kidney injury in myocardial infarction complicated by cardiogenic shock a retrospective observational study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Kun læseadgang","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ehjacc/zuaf048","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-830881","identifier":[{"id":"105013212512","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40165362","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-22b61783-884d-497a-8d1b-8a0f5e5be874"],"keyword":["Acute kidney injury","Acute myocardial infarction","Cardiogenic shock","Chronic kidney disease","Intensive care","Renal replacement therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-208336616DD445B97854C7B019F0798F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Kun læseadgang","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ehjacc/zuaf048","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"bjørnpau","last":"Bjørn","locid":"ec4eb74d-be08-4c91-88fe-adba012c248b","name":"Bjørn, Maria","orcid":"0009-0008-6916-8174","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joakim Bo","key":"kunkelpau","last":"Kunkel","name":"Kunkel, Joakim Bo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"helgestadpau","last":"Helgestad","locid":"ab9f3165-500c-482b-9c2f-1879b3abedb3","name":"Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","name_org":"Helgestad, Ole","orcid":"0000-0003-3847-8758","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"josiassenpau","last":"Josiassen","name":"Josiassen, Jakob","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karoline Korsholm","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"35431674-47f1-44be-a406-d01e49032afd","name":"Jeppesen, Karoline Korsholm","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"holmvangpau","last":"Holmvang","name":"Holmvang, Lene","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette Okkels","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil","key":"fosbølpau","last":"Fosbøl","name":"Fosbøl, Emil","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","name":"Hassager, Christian","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Berg","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"25de7650-3dc1-4594-b758-9c36f6de6306","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","orcid":"0000-0003-4702-5195","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40165362"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ehjacc/zuaf048","issn":["20488726","20488734"],"issn_org":["20488726"],"issue":"7","journal":"European Heart Journal: Acute Cardiovascular Care","pages":"385-391","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal: Acute Cardiovascular Care","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105013212512"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-22b61783-884d-497a-8d1b-8a0f5e5be874"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Long-term outcomes after acute kidney injury in myocardial infarction complicated by cardiogenic shock : A retrospective, observational study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-830881","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aims. Women continue to have a worse prognosis following ST-elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI) compared to men, despite advancements in treatment. This study investigates whether neurohormonal biomarker differences contribute to sex-related disparities in mortality. Methods and results. A total of 1892 consecutive STEMI patients from two tertiary heart centres were included. Admission neurohormonal activation defined as pro-atrial natriuretic peptide (proANP) and mid-regional pro-adrenomedullin (MR-proADM) was measured in blood drawn prior to acute coronary angiography (CAG). The primary endpoint was 1-year mortality stratified according to sex and biomarker level. Of 1782 (94%) with biomarkers available, 476 (27%) of patients were women. They were older (68 vs. 62 years), had longer symptom-to-angiography delay (211 vs. 181 min), and displayed a higher one-year mortality rate (12% vs. 7.4%, P < 0.001) compared to men. The neurohormonal response was higher in women compared to men [median (interquartile range) proANP 1050 (671–1591) vs. 772 (492–1294) pmol/L, P < 0.001); MR-proADM 0.80 (0.63–1.03) vs. 0.70 (0.58–0.89) nmol/L, P < 0.001]. In women, a level at or above the median was independently associated with a significantly higher mortality risk when adjusting for age, left ventricular ejection fraction, diabetes, heart failure, symptom onset to CAG, left-sided culprit lesion, obesity, renal dysfunction, primary percutaneous intervention, admission systolic blood pressure, and multivessel disease (HR proANP 6.05, 95% CI 1.81–20.3, P = 0.004; HR MR-proADM 3.49, 95% CI 1.42–8.62, P = 0.007). In men, there was an independent prognostic association for proANP but not for MR-proADM (HR proANP 2.38, 95% CI 1.18–4.81, P = 0.015; HR MR-proADM 1.74, 95% CI 0.89–3.40, P = 0.11). Conclusion. Increased neurohormonal activation (MR-proADM and proANP) is associated with higher mortality in women compared to men. Neurohormonal activation may contribute to the observed sex-related differences in mortality.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Kunkel, Joakim Bo","Søholm, Helle","Holle, Sarah L.D.","Goetze, Jens P.","Holmvang, Lene","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Sheikh, Annam P.","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Hassager, Christian","Frydland, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-802455"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Kunkel, Joakim Bo"],"keyword":["Adrenomedullin blood","Aged","Atrial Natriuretic Factor blood","Biomarkers","Biomarkers blood","Coronary Angiography","Female","Follow Up Studies","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Mortality","Neurohormonal activation","ProANP","Prognosis","Protein Precursors","ST Elevation Myocardial Infarction mortality","STEMI","Sex","Sex Factors","Survival Rate trends"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neurohormonal response is associated with mortality in women with st elevation myocardial infarction","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85216877983","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-802455","identifier":[{"id":"39657736","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85216877983","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-85a617f1-3a27-4840-bbf6-c2d1392c54fa"],"keyword":["Adrenomedullin/blood","Aged","Atrial Natriuretic Factor/blood","Biomarkers","Biomarkers/blood","Coronary Angiography","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","MR-proADM","Male","Middle Aged","Mortality","Neurohormonal activation","ProANP","Prognosis","Protein Precursors","ST Elevation Myocardial Infarction/mortality","STEMI","Sex","Sex Factors","Survival Rate/trends"],"lang":"English