{"abstract":"Objective: Beyond glucose-lowering, sodium-glucose co-transporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitors have cardioprotective effects with unclear mechanisms. We examined changes in an extensive panel of plasma lipids, lipoproteins, and apolipoproteins and whether these changes were independent of weight loss, hemoglobin A1c, and hematocrit in patients treated with empagliflozin versus placebo to better understand the observed cardioprotective effects. Methods: Post-hoc analyses of two double-blind, placebo-controlled trials, the Empire HF trial including 190 patients with heart failure and reduced ejection fraction and the SIMPLE trial including 90 patients with type 2 diabetes randomized to, respectively, 10 mg and 25 mg empagliflozin daily or placebo for 12 weeks. Results: In studies combined, empagliflozin reduced age and sex adjusted body weight by 1.40 kg (SEM: 0.10; p < 0.001) and hemoglobin A1c by 2.71 mmol/mol (SEM: 0.24; p < 0.001); and increased hematocrit by 1.9% (SEM: 0.12; p < 0.001) compared to placebo. No mean changes were seen in concentrations of total cholesterol, low-density lipoprotein (LDL) cholesterol, small dense LDL cholesterol, very low-density lipoprotein cholesterol, triglyceride rich lipoprotein cholesterol, non-high-density lipoprotein (non-HDL) cholesterol, apolipoprotein B, lipoprotein(a), HDL cholesterol, and triglycerides adjusted for body weight, hemoglobin A1c, and hematocrit with empagliflozin compared to placebo. Conclusion: Empagliflozin treatment reduced body weight and hemoglobin A1c; and increased hematocrit. No changes were seen in concentrations of lipids and lipoproteins with empagliflozin compared to placebo. This suggests that the cardioprotective effects of SGLT2 inhibitors are independent of lipid and lipoprotein concentrations.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Emanuelsson, Frida","Jensen, Jesper","Omar, Massar","Jürgens, Mikkel","Kistorp, Caroline","Brandt-Jacobsen, Niels H.","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Schou, Morten","Bechmann, Louise Ellegaard","Larsen, Emil List","Nordestgaard, Børge G","Benn, Marianne"],"cuid":["S02-099.76-804529"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Benn, Marianne"],"keyword":["Aged","Benzhydryl Compounds therapeutic use","Cholesterol","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 drug therapy","Double Blind Method","Female","Glucosides therapeutic use","Glycated Hemoglobin metabolism","Heart Failure blood","Heart failure","Humans","Lipids blood","Lipoprotein a","Lipoproteins blood","Male","Middle Aged","Sodium Glucose Transporter 2 Inhibitors","Sodium glucose cotransporter 2 inhibition","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of empagliflozin on plasma lipids and lipoproteins in type 000000000002 diabetes and heart failure empire hf and simple","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jacl.2024.12.015","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.76-804529","identifier":[{"id":"85215621142","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39843293","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a68b67aa-530a-46a6-9b9c-335bf311e49f","sdu-d5656762-a65b-4a1c-8e2c-fb1f492a0298"],"keyword":["Aged","Benzhydryl Compounds/therapeutic use","Cholesterol","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/drug therapy","Double-Blind Method","Female","Glucosides/therapeutic use","Glycated Hemoglobin/metabolism","Heart Failure/blood","Heart failure","Humans","Lipids/blood","Lipoprotein(a)","Lipoproteins/blood","Male","Middle Aged","Sodium-Glucose Transporter 2 Inhibitors","Sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibition","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EE0A8ACB82D16F5B055465ED2D4F624C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/448972853/1-s2.0-S1933287424003039-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jacl.2024.12.015","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/288661797/1-s2.0-S1933287424003039-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of SDCO - Steno Diabetes Center Odense"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku 