rd","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 1","first":"Jeppe K.","key":"petersenjeppekpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Jeppe K.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 1","first":"Eva","key":"haversborgersenevapau","last":"Havers-Borgersen","name":"Havers-Borgersen, Eva","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jannik","key":"helweglarsenjannikpau","last":"Helweg-Larsen","name":"Helweg-Larsen, Jannik","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Daniel","key":"faurholtjepsendanielpau","last":"Faurholt-Jepsen","locid":"789d8552-3f68-48cf-b78a-f616c0cd62b5","name":"Faurholt-Jepsen, Daniel","orcid":"0000-0001-8561-0155","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Henning","key":"bundgaardhenningpau","last":"Bundgaard","locid":"254c7f8d-79dd-4a5d-870f-3ed78cb56464","name":"Bundgaard, Henning","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Kasper","key":"iversenkasperpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"558df261-ca9f-440a-8bee-7d38813c253f","name":"Iversen, Kasper","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lauge","key":"østergaardlaugepau","last":"Østergaard","name":"Østergaard, Lauge","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Lars","key":"køberlarspau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Emil L.","key":"fosbølemilpau","last":"Fosbøl","locid":"3089319b-8ca3-4959-8e4a-072bdb702871","name":"Fosbøl, Emil","name_org":"Fosbøl, Emil L.","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39954837"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ahj.2025.02.006","issn":["00028703","10976744"],"issn_org":["00028703"],"journal":"American Heart Journal","pages":"119-132","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"American Heart Journal","volume":"285"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001487948"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e3871eab-4118-428e-8f08-6e3a4ed7d83b","au-ee54c56b-621d-4606-8b21-4b206ad155fd","ku-5c34b3dc-9f94-4f96-b10d-165f719ec159","sdu-355c074b-cf4b-40ca-8aee-a4f9a5339219"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Patient characteristics, presentation, causal microorganisms, and overall mortality in the NatIonal Danish endocarditis stUdieS (NIDUS) registry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-803859","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: In mechanically ventilated adult patients in the intensive care unit (ICU), selective decontamination of the digestive tract (SDD) has been shown to reduce the risk of infections and improve survival. While the benefits of SDD have been documented in this population, it remains unclear whether burn patients, who are at increased risk of infection and have distinct clinical characteristics, may experience similar benefits. In this systematic review we aimed to assess the desirable and undesirable patient-important effects of administering SDD to burn patients. Methods/design: We conducted a systematic review with meta-analysis of randomized clinical trials (RCTs) assessing the effects of SDD versus placebo or no SDD in burn patients. The primary outcome was 30-day mortality. Secondary outcomes included serious adverse events, antimicrobial resistance, pneumonia, blood stream infections, ICU- and hospital-free days, and 90-day mortality. We searched all major databases and followed the recommendations provided by the Cochrane Collaboration and the Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analyses guidelines. The certainty of evidence was assessed according to the Grading of Recommendations Assessment, Development, and Evaluation approach. Results: We identified four RCTs with a total of 457 burn patients. All trials were assessed as having either ‘some concerns’ or ‘high risk’ of bias. The evidence was found to be very uncertain across all outcomes assessed. For mortality, the relative risk (RR) was 0.62 (95 % confidence interval (CI) 0.22–1.78, I2 = 75 %, random-effects model (REM), very low certainty evidence). For pneumonia, the RR was 0.75 (95 % CI 0.48–1.19, I2 = 0 %, fixed-effect model, very low certainty evidence). For bloodstream infections, the RR was 1.10 (95 % CI 0.71–1.69, I2 = 0 %, REM, very low certainty evidence). For hospital length of stay, the mean difference was −2.03 days (95 % CI −9.64–5.59, I2 = 51 %, REM, very low certainty evidence). We did not perform meta-analyses for the remaining secondary outcomes due to limited or no data. Trial sequential analysis could not be performed due to insufficient number of total participants and events in the included trials. Conclusion: We found that the certainty of evidence is very low about the effects of SDD on patient-important outcomes in burn patients. Extrapolating from the evidence on mechanically ventilated adult ICU patients may be reasonable until more data from RCTs in burn patients emerge.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Tsuchiya, Emma Atsuko","Jensen-Abbew, Jacob","Krag, Mette","Møller, Morten Hylander","Vestergaard, Martin Risom","Haase, Nicolai","Helleberg, Marie","Holmgaard, Rikke","Heiberg, Johan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-810882"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Antibiotic prophylaxis","Bacteremia","Burns","Gastrointestinal tract","Infections","Pneumonia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"selective decontamination of the digestive tract in burn patients a systematic review with meta analysis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.burns.2025.107501","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-810882","identifier":[{"id":"105002698085","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40250196","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-bcc91c40-8495-4de8-aca0-cc9809e3f68e"],"keyword":["antibiotic prophylaxis","bacteremia","burns","gastrointestinal tract","infections","pneumonia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B0FDBB99021C6C79A83FFD4F6E6CD0BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.burns.2025.107501","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/447849592/1-s2.0-S0305417925001305-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Emma Atsuko","key":"tsuchiyapau","last":"Tsuchiya","locid":"4a197aaf-48d4-4a2e-a2ff-86d52a7081ee","name":"Tsuchiya, Emma Atsuko","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jacob","key":"jensenabbewpau","last":"Jensen-Abbew","name":"Jensen-Abbew, Jacob","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mette","key":"kragpau","last":"Krag","locid":"de08c219-be19-41c9-94b6-474ec53a7a46","name":"Krag, Mette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Morten Hylander","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"9463b017-3c43-470d-b95b-cf3cba8a27d4","name":"Møller, Morten Hylander","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Martin Risom","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","name":"Vestergaard, Martin Risom","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nicolai","key":"haasepau","last":"Haase","name":"Haase, Nicolai","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marie","key":"hellebergpau","last":"Helleberg","name":"Helleberg, Marie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rikke","key":"holmgaardpau","last":"Holmgaard","name":"Holmgaard, Rikke","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Johan","key":"heibergpau","last":"Heiberg","locid":"55e3a411-514f-4702-a534-102039744183","name":"Heiberg, Johan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40250196"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.burns.2025.107501","issn":["03054179","18791409"],"issn_org":["03054179"],"issue":"5","journal":"Burns","paperid":"107501","status":"p","title":"Burns","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105002698085"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bcc91c40-8495-4de8-aca0-cc9809e3f68e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Selective decontamination of the digestive tract in burn patients : A systematic review with meta-analysis","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-810882","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aims Liver injury is a frequent complication in patients with acute myocardial infarction complicated by cardiogenic shock (AMICS). The model for end-stage liver disease incorporating albumin (MELD-albumin) quantifies liver injury. This study assesses the association between MELD-albumin score and all-cause mortality among patients with AMICS. Methods From a retrospective cohort of 1716 consecutive patients with AMICS admitted between 2010 and 2017, we included pa- and results tients who survived until Day 3 and had complete laboratory data available (n = 717). The MELD-albumin was calculated using 0 to 72 h peak s-bilirubin and s-creatinine values and the lowest s-albumin value. Patients were stratified into tertiles: low, intermediate, and high MELD-albumin. The primary outcome was all-cause mortality with a follow-up of up to 14 years. Patients in the high-score group were more often female, had lower left ventricular ejection fraction, had higher lactate levels, and less suffered out-of-hospital cardiac arrest. The high-score group had a significantly higher all-cause mortality rate than the intermediate- and low-score groups at 30 days (49 vs. 35 vs. 26%, P < 0.001) and 10 years for 30-day survivors (58 vs. 46 vs. 37%, P < 0.001). Adjusted hazard ratios for mortality in the high-score group were 2.02 at 30 days [95% confidence interval (CI): 1.49–2.74, P < 0.001] and 1.86 at 10 years (95% CI: 1.18–2.92, P < 0.001). The MELD-albumin score demonstrated an area under the receiver operating curve of 0.63 (95% CI: 0.59–0.67) for predicting 30-day mortality. Conclusion Liver injury, quantified as MELD-albumin score, was significantly associated with short- and long-term all-cause mortality among patients with AMICS.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Alaoui-Ismaili, Zakaria","Kunkel, Joakim Bo","Klein, Anika","Josiassen, Jakob","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Jeppesen, Karoline Korsholm","Schmidt, Henrik","Holmvang, Lene","Graversen, Peter Laursen","Fosbøl, Emil","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-831063"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Alaoui-Ismaili, Zakaria"],"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction","Albumin","Cardiogenic shock","Liver injury","Model for end stage liver disease","Mortality"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"model for end stage liver disease incorporating albumin score is associated with short and long term all cause mortality in patients with acute myocardial infarction complicated by cardiogenic shock","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105010235611","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-831063","identifier":[{"id":"40265664","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105010235611","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-5691bf16-97f6-41ae-abe4-7166dfa0526c"],"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction","Albumin","Cardiogenic shock","Liver injury","Model for end-stage liver disease","Mortality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-94B0BD28D7FCDF63FE74A50386F2FC34"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zakaria","key":"alaouiismailipau","last":"Alaoui-Ismaili","name":"Alaoui-Ismaili, Zakaria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joakim Bo","key":"kunkelpau","last":"Kunkel","name":"Kunkel, Joakim Bo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anika","key":"kleinpau","last":"Klein","name":"Klein, Anika","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"josiassenpau","last":"Josiassen","name":"Josiassen, Jakob","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole Kristian","key":"lerchehelgestadpau","last":"Lerche Helgestad","locid":"ab9f3165-500c-482b-9c2f-1879b3abedb3","name":"Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","name_org":"Lerche Helgestad, Ole Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-3847-8758","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karoline Korsholm","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"35431674-47f1-44be-a406-d01e49032afd","name":"Jeppesen, Karoline Korsholm","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"holmvangpau","last":"Holmvang","name":"Holmvang, Lene","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Laursen","key":"graversenpau","last":"Graversen","name":"Graversen, Peter Laursen","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil","key":"fosbølpau","last":"Fosbøl","name":"Fosbøl, Emil","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Berg","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"25de7650-3dc1-4594-b758-9c36f6de6306","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","orcid":"0000-0003-4702-5195","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette Okkels","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","name":"Hassager, Christian","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40265664"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ehjacc/zuaf063","issn":["20488726","20488734"],"issn_org":["20488726"],"issue":"6","journal":"European Heart Journal: Acute Cardiovascular Care","pages":"342-350","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal: Acute Cardiovascular Care","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105010235611"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-5691bf16-97f6-41ae-abe4-7166dfa0526c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Model for end-stage liver disease incorporating albumin score is associated with short- and long-term all-cause mortality in patients with acute myocardial infarction complicated by cardiogenic shock","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-831063","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Low systolic blood pressure (SBP) is a key criterion for diagnosing cardiogenic shock (CS) caused by a reduction in stroke volume and cardiac output (CO). The temporal interaction between changes in pressure and flow has not been well described in the development of CS. In a large animal model, we assessed the temporal relationships of SBP, CO, and blood flow in the carotid artery during induction of CS. Methods: Fifteen adult Danish landrace pigs (median weight 71 kg) underwent CS induction by stepwise injection of polyvinyl alcohol microspheres into the left main coronary artery every 3 min to induce microvascular obstruction. After each injection, CO, SBP, and mixed venous saturation (SvO2) were recorded simultaneously from a ventricle sheath in the carotid artery and a pulmonary artery catheter in the right internal jugular vein. A Doppler flow probe measured blood flow in the left carotid artery. CS was defined as a ≥ 50% reduction in CO or SvO2 from baseline, or absolute SvO2 < 30%. Results: CS occurred after a mean of 8 (range 5 to 19) boluses of microspheres. SBP declined from 99 (± 15) mmHg to 74 (± 6) mmHg, equal to 74 (± 13)% of the baseline value. CO was reduced to 5.8 (± 0.7) L/min to 2.2 (± 1.3) L/min, equal to 38 (± 23)% and SvO2 from 63 (± 7)% to 37 (± 7)%, equal to 60 (± 13)% of baseline values. The decrease in CO was due to a reduction to 43 (± 26)% in stroke volume, as heart rate remained unchanged. The carotid artery blood flow was reduced from 285 (± 50) mL/min to 155 (± 56) mL/min, equal to 54% of baseline values. The decline in SvO2 and CO preceded a reduction in SBP, and after 25% of emboli were given, CO decreased by 24% while SBP was unchanged. Conclusion: In a porcine model of ischemic myocardial injury, the decrease in blood flow and stroke volume preceded a decline in SBP, suggesting pressure preservation occurs in the presence of hypoperfusion.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Svanekjaer, Laura","Larsen, Jeppe P.","Frederiksen, Peter H.","Linde, Louise","Gregers, Emilie","Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Banke, Ann","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Lassen, Jens Flensted","Povlsen, Amalie Ling","Schmidt, Henrik","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Ravn, Hanne Berg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-831307"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Svanekjaer, Laura"],"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction","Arterial blood pressure","Cardiac Output","Cardiogenic shock","Hypoperfusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of changes in arterial blood pressure and cardiac output during cardiogenic shock development in a porcine model","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40635-025-00802-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-831307","identifier":[{"id":"105014915344","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12401854","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40889089","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-99c6c123-241b-4b77-aae6-6fc0de41d621"],"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction","Arterial blood pressure","Cardiac output","Cardiogenic shock","Hypoperfusion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-A2597EA45DFD594B8C24319AC41E8882"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/296110677/s40635-025-00802-3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40635-025-00802-3","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"svanekjaerpau","last":"Svanekjaer","name":"Svanekjaer, Laura","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe K.P.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9c1f7b9d-9e43-45ec-aa4d-310cdce6686a","name":"Larsen, Jeppe P.","name_org":"Larsen, Jeppe K.P.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter H.","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"85d6facd-93bf-44ee-a117-269fb26a52be","name":"Frederiksen, Peter H.","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-7980","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"lindepau","last":"Linde","locid":"4fc23628-00d4-466a-9e6e-269e23160481","name":"Linde, Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-7757-2571","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Emilie","key":"gregerspau","last":"Gregers","name":"Gregers, Emilie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna L.J.","key":"udesenpau","last":"Udesen","locid":"f71f56f5-4f36-4de5-a7ae-e5e51f101a83","name":"Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","name_org":"Udesen, Nanna L.J.","orcid":"0000-0003-1542-3260","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole K.","key":"helgestadpau","last":"Helgestad","locid":"ab9f3165-500c-482b-9c2f-1879b3abedb3","name":"Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","name_org":"Helgestad, Ole K.","orcid":"0000-0003-3847-8758","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann","key":"bankepau","last":"Banke","locid":"0d350637-c6ce-4cf8-82ba-e965da703690","name":"Banke, Ann","orcid":"0000-0002-1036-580X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette O.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","name_org":"Jensen, Lisette O.","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens F.","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"2af194b2-635f-4b62-84c2-26bd7dc3263b","name":"Lassen, Jens Flensted","name_org":"Lassen, Jens F.","orcid":"0000-0001-7972-9192","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Amalie L.","key":"povlsenpau","last":"Povlsen","locid":"085efe15-36a1-434b-9b9e-b4341cd84a0d","name":"Povlsen, Amalie Ling","name_org":"Povlsen, Amalie L.","orcid":"0000-0001-6044-8841","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob E.","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","name_org":"Møller, Jacob E.","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne B.","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"25de7650-3dc1-4594-b758-9c36f6de6306","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","name_org":"Ravn, Hanne B.","orcid":"0000-0003-4702-5195","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40889089"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s40635-025-00802-3","issn":["2197425X"],"journal":"Intensive Care Medicine Experimental","paperid":"91","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Intensive Care Medicine Experimental","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105014915344"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-99c6c123-241b-4b77-aae6-6fc0de41d621"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Comparison of changes in arterial blood pressure and cardiac output during cardiogenic shock development in a porcine model","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-831307","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background Butyrate, a short-chain fatty acid, has shown potential to improve left ventricular (LV) function and induce vasorelaxation in rodents. Butyrate may either be produced by the microbiome in the colon, be ingested or administered intravenously. This study aimed to evaluate effects of butyrate on cardiac output (CO) and associated hemodynamic variables in a porcine model. Methods In a randomized, blinded crossover study, ten healthy 60-kg pigs were given three-hour infusions of 600 mM butyrate and equimolar sodium chloride (control). CO was measured by thermodilution via a pulmonary artery catheter. LV contractility was assessed using pressure-volume admittance catheterization. Additionally, isolated porcine coronary arteries were exposed to butyrate in a wire myograph to evaluate vasorelaxation. Results Butyrate infusion increased plasma butyrate concentration to 0.53 mM (95% confidence interval (CI): 0.49 to 0.58 mM, P<0.001) and CO by 1.6 L/min (95% CI: 1.0 to 2.1 L/min, P<0.001) compared with the control. Heart rate, LV ejection fraction, cardiac efficiency and dP/dtmax rose, while systemic vascular resistance, arterial elastance, mean arterial pressure and LV ends-systolic volume decreased. Load-independent LV contractility and stroke volume did not significantly differ. In the myograph, porcine coronary arteries relaxed in response to butyrate in a concentration-dependent manner. Conclusion Butyrate increased CO by lowering systemic vascular tone and raising heart rate. Although load-independent contractility remained stable, increased dP/dtmax and ejection fraction, preserved stroke volume and decreased LV end-systolic volume indicated an enhanced cardiac contractile performance. These cardiovascular effects of butyrate warrant further clinical investigation.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Larsen, Alexander Møller","Christensen, Lasse Juul","Homilius, Casper","Gopalasingam, Nigopan","Moeslund, Niels","Berg-Hansen, Kristoffer","Boedtkjer, Ebbe","Jensen, Rebekka Vibjerg","Johannsen, Mogens","Hansen, Jakob","Seefeldt, Jacob Marthinsen","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Schütz, Julian","Hørsdal, Oskar Kjærgaard","Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-807014"],"event":{"end":"2025-03-15","place":"Firenze, it","start":"2025-03-14","title":"European Society of Cardiology: Acute CardioVascular Care Congress 2025","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"butyrate increases cardiac output and causes vasorelaxation in a healthy porcine model","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-807014","ids":["au-93da2d2d-31a8-4567-906d-0281d8f44403"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-6D7E5D9F7C1404062E059F18A744694A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alexander Møller","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"c597eab5-5b08-4c91-ae6f-d25e64c92d74","name":"Larsen, Alexander Møller","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lasse Juul","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"d4e027d7-5bf2-445d-970c-815957cd7d10","name":"Christensen, Lasse Juul","orcid":"0009-0002-4997-5901","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","correspondi