{"abstract":"Background: The clinical spectrum of acute myocardial infarction complicated by cardiogenic shock (AMICS) varies. Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) can be the first sign of cardiac failure, whereas others present with various degrees of hemodynamic instability (non-OHCA). The aim of the present study was to explore differences in prehospital management and characteristics of survivors and nonsurvivors in AMICS patients with OHCA or non-OHCA. Methods: Data analysis was based on patient data from the RETROSHOCK cohort comprising consecutive AMICS patients admitted to two tertiary cardiac centers between 2010 and 2017. Results: 1,716 AMICS patientswere included and 42%presented withOHCA.Mortality inOHCApatients was 47% versus 57%in the non-OHCA group. Almost all OHCA patients were intubated before admission (96%). In the non-OHCA group, prehospital intubation (25%) was associated with a better survival (P < 0.001). Lactate level on admission demonstrated a linear relationship with mortality in OHCA patients. In non-OHCA, probability of death was higher for any given lactate level <12 mmol/L compared with OHCA. However, a lactate level >7 mmol/L in non-OHCA did not increasemortality odds any further. Conclusion: Mortality was almost doubled for any admission lactate level up to 7 mmol/L in non-OHCA patients. Above this level, mortality remained unchanged in non-OHCA patients but continued to increase in OHCA patients. Prehospital intubation was performed in almost all OHCA patients but only in one of four patients without OHCA. Early intubation in non-OHCA patients was associated with a better outcome.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Beck Mieritz, Hanne","Povlsen, Amalie Ling","Linde, Louise","Beske, Rasmus Paulin","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Josiassen, Jakob","Hassager, C","Schmidt, Henrik","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Holmvang, L","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Ravn, Hanne Berg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-733568"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Beck Mieritz, Hanne"],"keyword":["Cardiogenic shock","Humans","Lactate","Lactates","Mechanical ventilation","Myocardial Infarction","Myocardial Infarction complications","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest therapy","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Shock Cardiogenic etiology","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"differences in management and prognostication of cardiogenic shock patients in the presence and absence of out of hospital cardiac arrest","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85186265069","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-733568","identifier":[{"id":"38010103","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85186265069","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-1f555436-72c0-44a1-84ec-c5a35f726845"],"keyword":["Cardiogenic shock","Humans","Lactates","Myocardial Infarction/complications","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest/therapy","Shock, Cardiogenic/etiology","Treatment Outcome","lactate","mechanical ventilation","myocardial infarction","out-of-hospital cardiac arrest"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BA3B81BFA913A263F5EB6EEC564E6C52"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"HB","key":"mieritzpau","last":"Mieritz","locid":"9f6e0386-ac47-431c-86ef-abbd91c87a14","name":"Beck Mieritz, Hanne","name_org":"Mieritz, HB","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amalie Ling","key":"povlsenpau","last":"Povlsen","locid":"085efe15-36a1-434b-9b9e-b4341cd84a0d","name":"Povlsen, Amalie Ling","orcid":"0000-0001-6044-8841","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L","key":"lindepau","last":"Linde","locid":"4fc23628-00d4-466a-9e6e-269e23160481","name":"Linde, Louise","name_org":"Linde, L","orcid":"0000-0002-7757-2571","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Paulin","key":"beskepau","last":"Beske","name":"Beske, Rasmus Paulin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"OKL","key":"helgestadpau","last":"Helgestad","locid":"ab9f3165-500c-482b-9c2f-1879b3abedb3","name":"Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","name_org":"Helgestad, OKL","orcid":"0000-0003-3847-8758","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"josiassenpau","last":"Josiassen","name":"Josiassen, Jakob","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"C","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","name":"Hassager, C","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"H","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","name_org":"Schmidt, H","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"LO","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","name_org":"Jensen, LO","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"L","key":"holmvangpau","last":"Holmvang","name":"Holmvang, L","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"JE","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","name_org":"Møller, JE","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"HB","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"25de7650-3dc1-4594-b758-9c36f6de6306","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","name_org":"Ravn, HB","orcid":"0000-0003-4702-5195","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38010103"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/shk.0000000000002272","issn":["10732322","15400514"],"issn_org":["10732322"],"issue":"2","journal":"Shock","pages":"209-214","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Shock","title_org":"Shock (Augusta, Ga.)","volume":"61"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85186265069"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-1f555436-72c0-44a1-84ec-c5a35f726845"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Differences in management and prognostication of Cardiogenic Shock patients in the presence and absence of Out-of-hospital Cardiac arrest.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-733568","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Acute kidney injury (AKI) is a significant risk factor associated with reduced survival following out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA). Whether the severity of AKI simply serves as a surrogate measure of worse peri-arrest conditions, or represents an additional risk to long-term survival remains unclear. METHODS: This is a sub-study derived from a randomized trial in which 789 comatose adult OHCA patients with presumed cardiac cause and sustained return of spontaneous circulation (ROSC) were enrolled. Patients without prior dialysis dependent kidney disease and surviving at least 48 h were included (N = 759). AKI was defined by the kidney disease: improving global outcome (KDIGO) classification, and patients were divided into groups based on the development of AKI and the need for continuous kidney replacement therapy (CKRT), thus establishing three groups of patients-No AKI, AKI no CKRT, and AKI CKRT. Primary outcome was overall survival within 365 days after OHCA according to AKI group. Adjusted Cox proportional hazard models were used to assess overall survival within 365 days according to the three groups. RESULTS: In the whole population, median age was 64 (54-73) years, 80% male, 90% of patients presented with shockable rhythm, and time to ROSC was median 18 (12-26) min. A total of 254 (33.5%) patients developed AKI according to the KDIGO definition, with 77 requiring CKRT and 177 without need for CKRT. AKI CKRT patients had longer time-to-ROSC and worse metabolic derangement at hospital admission. Overall survival within 365 days from OHCA decreased with the severity of kidney injury. Adjusted Cox regression analysis found that AKI, both with and without CKRT, was significantly associated with reduced overall survival up until 365 days, with comparable hazard ratios relative to no AKI (HR 1.75, 95% CI 1.13-2.70 vs. HR 1.76, 95% CI 1.30-2.39). CONCLUSIONS: In comatose patients who had been resuscitated after OHCA, patients developing AKI, with or without initiation of CKRT, had a worse 1-year overall survival compared to non-AKI patients. This association remains statistically significant after adjusting for other peri-arrest risk factors. TRIAL REGISTRATION: The BOX trial is registered at ClinicalTrials.gov: NCT03141099.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Jeppesen, Karoline Korsholm","Rasmussen, Sebastian Buhl","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Schmidt, Henrik","Mølstrøm, Simon","Beske, Rasmus Paulin","Grand, Johannes","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Meyer, Martin Abild Stengaard","Hassager, Christian","Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"cuid":["S02-087.23-785500"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"keyword":["Acute Kidney Injury therapy","Acute kidney injury","Aged","Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest therapy","Post cardiac arrest","Proportional Hazards Models"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"acute kidney injury after out of hospital cardiac arrest","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-024-04936-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.23-785500","identifier":[{"id":"38762578","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11102609","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85193546698","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bbe61848-31a2-4261-a0e5-ba6adbaf17f6","sdu-eedf69ed-0d3a-4394-b49d-1e3f3065cd13"],"keyword":["Acute Kidney Injury/therapy","Acute kidney injury","Aged","Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Continuous kidney replacement therapy","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest/therapy","Post-cardiac arrest","Proportional Hazards Models"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DE68FD18347D452535FA9C3639B4B5D2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/260536469/s13054-024-04936-w.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/420928675/s13054_024_04936_w.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-024-04936-w","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karoline Korsholm","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"35431674-47f1-44be-a406-d01e49032afd","name":"Jeppesen, Karoline Korsholm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Buhl","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ab6fae27-1823-419c-94e5-9fd43df69e74","name":"Rasmussen, Sebastian Buhl","orcid":"0000-0002-3990-2197","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"10ffadd9-ed9c-4251-954a-a2c12ce83aca","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"mølstrømpau","last":"Mølstrøm","locid":"197d79e9-dd07-401b-90f8-1c26dc359db2","name":"Mølstrøm, Simon","orcid":"0000-0002-2778-8075","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Paulin","key":"beskepau","last":"Beske","name":"Beske, Rasmus Paulin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Johannes","key":"grandpau","last":"Grand","name":"Grand, Johannes","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Berg","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"25de7650-3dc1-4594-b758-9c36f6de6306","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","orcid":"0000-0003-4702-5195","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Matilde","key":"wintherjensenpau","last":"Winther-Jensen","name":"Winther-Jensen, Matilde","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Abild Stengaard","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Martin Abild Stengaard","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38762578"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13054-024-04936-w","issn":["1466609X"],"issn_org":["13648535"],"issue":"1","journal":"Critical Care","paperid":"169","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Critical Care","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85193546698"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bbe61848-31a2-4261-a0e5-ba6adbaf17f6","sdu-eedf69ed-0d3a-4394-b49d-1e3f3065cd13"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Acute kidney injury after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.23-785500","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background The relationship between speckle tracking assessed global longitudinal strain (GLS) and Doppler-based echocardiography with basic physiological markers of cardiac function derived from pressure-volume loops is poorly elucidated. Objective We aimed to describe the association between LS and Doppler-based echocardiography and direct measurements of central haemodynamic parameters from conductance catheter-based pressure-volume loops in an animal model with increasing left ventricular (LV) dysfunction. Methods 12 Danish landrace female pigs (75-80 kg) were used. All instrumentations were performed percutaneously, including the conductance catheter in the LV. Progressive LV dysfunction was induced by embolisation through the left main coronary artery with microspheres every 3 min until a >50% reduction in cardiac output (CO) or mixed venous saturation (SvO 2), compared with baseline, or SvO 2 <30%. Echocardiography was performed at baseline and 90 s after each injection. Results With progressive LV dysfunction, mean CO decreased from 5.6±0.9 L/min to 2.1±0.9 L/min, and mean SvO 2 deteriorated from 61.1±7.9% to 35.3±6.1%. Mean LS and LV outflow tract velocity time integral (LVOT VTI) declined from -13.8±3.0% to -6.1±2.0% and 16.9±2.6 cm to 7.8±1.8 cm, respectively. LS and LVOT VTI showed the strongest correlation to stroke work in unadjusted linear regression (r 2 =0.53 and r 2 =0.49, respectively). LS correlated significantly with stroke volume, end-systolic elastance, systolic blood pressure, ventriculo-arterial coupling and arterial elastance. Conclusion In an animal model of acute progressive LV dysfunction, echocardiographic and conductance catheter-based measurements changed significantly. LS and LVOT VTI displayed the earliest and the largest alterations with increased myocardial damage and both correlated strongest with stroke work.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Peter H.","Linde, Louise","Gregers, Emilie","Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Banke, Ann","Dahl, Jordi Sanchez","Povlsen, Amalie Ling","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Larsen, Jeppe P.","Lassen, Jens Flensted","Schmidt, Henrik","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-750924"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Frederiksen, Peter H."],"keyword":["Acute coronary syndrome","Animals","Disease Models Animal","Echocardiography","Echocardiography Doppler methods","Female","Heart failure","Predictive Value of Tests","Shock Cardiogenic physiopathology","Swine","Ventricular Dysfunction Left physiopathology","Ventricular Function Left physiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between speckle tracking echocardiography and pressure volume loops during cardiogenic shock development","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/openhrt-2023-002512","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-750924","identifier":[{"id":"85195036305","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38782543","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11116883","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-c49e3ce8-e862-478b-9a64-f707bfb9ade6"],"keyword":["Acute Coronary Syndrome","Animals","Disease Models, Animal","Echocardiography","Echocardiography, Doppler/methods","Female","Heart Failure","Predictive Value of Tests","Shock, Cardiogenic/physiopathology","Swine","Ventricular Dysfunction, Left/physiopathology","Ventricular Function, Left/physiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-03E98CBDF94A2BF2111320053E2775F3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"C