{"abstract":"Background: Nosocomial infections contribute significantly to mortality and morbidity in burn patients. Selective decontamination of the digestive tract is an infection prevention measure that has been shown to improve survival in mechanically ventilated intensive care unit (ICU) patients. It has been hypothesized that burn patients may benefit from selective decontamination of the digestive tract. Methods/Design: We will conduct a systematic review with meta-analysis and trial sequential analysis of randomized clinical trials (RCTs) assessing the patient-important effects of selective decontamination of the digestive tract in burn patients, as compared with placebo or no intervention/standard of care. The primary outcome will be 30-day mortality. Secondary outcomes include serious adverse events, anti-microbial resistance, pneumonia, blood stream infections, ICU- and hospital-free days and 90-day mortality. We will search the following databases: CENTRAL, MEDLINE, EMBASE, BIOSIS, Web of Science and CINAHL and follow the recommendations provided by the Cochrane Collaboration and the Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analyses guidelines. The certainty of evidence will be assessed according to the GRADE approach: Grading of Recommendations Assessment, Development and Evaluation. Discussion: There is clinical equipoise about the use of selective decontamination of the digestive tract in burn patients. In the outlined systematic review and meta-analysis, we will assess the desirable and undesirable effects of selective decontamination of the digestive tract in burn patients.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Tsuchiya, Emma Atsuko","Jensen-Abbew, Jacob","Krag, Mette","Møller, Morten Hylander","Vestergaard, Martin Risom","Overgaard-Steensen, Christian","Helleberg, Marie","Holmgaard, Rikke","Heiberg, Johan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-778665"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Burns"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"selective decontamination of the digestive tract in burn patients protocol for a systematic review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14498","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-778665","identifier":[{"id":"85197769839","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38981497","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a794655c-11f8-4650-9772-9162b3ef8901"],"keyword":["anti-biotic prophylaxis","burns","selective digestive decontamination"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-24632C23CBF2D00691AF3A1BB65CA130"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14498","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/411776542/Acta_Anaesthesiol_Scand_2024_Tsuchiya_Selective_decontamination_of_the_digestive_tract_in_burn_patients_Protocol_for.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Emma Atsuko","key":"tsuchiyapau","last":"Tsuchiya","name":"Tsuchiya, Emma Atsuko","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"jensenabbewpau","last":"Jensen-Abbew","name":"Jensen-Abbew, Jacob","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mette","key":"kragpau","last":"Krag","locid":"de08c219-be19-41c9-94b6-474ec53a7a46","name":"Krag, Mette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Morten Hylander","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"9463b017-3c43-470d-b95b-cf3cba8a27d4","name":"Møller, Morten Hylander","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin Risom","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","name":"Vestergaard, Martin Risom","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"overgaardsteensenpau","last":"Overgaard-Steensen","name":"Overgaard-Steensen, Christian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Marie","key":"hellebergpau","last":"Helleberg","locid":"396ba4df-d603-4863-82c2-470006379976","name":"Helleberg, Marie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rikke","key":"holmgaardpau","last":"Holmgaard","name":"Holmgaard, Rikke","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Johan","key":"heibergpau","last":"Heiberg","locid":"55e3a411-514f-4702-a534-102039744183","name":"Heiberg, Johan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38981497"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.14498","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"10","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"1549-1555","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197769839"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a794655c-11f8-4650-9772-9162b3ef8901"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Selective decontamination of the digestive tract in burn patients : Protocol for a systematic review","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-778665","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Veno-arterial extracorporeal membrane oxygenation (VA-ECMO) with profound left ventricular (LV) failure is associated with inadequate LV emptying. To unload the LV, VA-ECMO can be combined with Impella CP (ECMELLA). We hypothesized that ECMELLA improves cardiac energetics compared with VA-ECMO in a porcine model of cardiogenic shock (CS). METHODS AND RESULTS: Land-race pigs (weight 70 kg) were instrumented, including a LV conductance catheter and a carotid artery Doppler flow probe. CS was induced with embolization in the left main coronary artery. CS was defined as reduction of ≥50% in cardiac output or mixed oxygen saturation (SvO 2) or a SvO 2 < 30%. At CS VA-ECMO was initiated and embolization was continued until arterial pulse pressure was <10 mmHg. At this point, Impella CP was placed in the ECMELLA arm. Support was maintained for 4 h. CS was induced in 15 pigs (VA-ECMO n = 7, ECMELLA n = 8). At time of CS MAP was <45 mmHg in both groups, with no difference at 4 h (VA-ECMO 64 mmHg ± 11 vs. ECMELLA 55 mmHg ± 21, P = 0.08). Carotid blood flow and arterial lactate increased from CS and was similar in VA-ECMO and ECMELLA [239 mL/min ± 97 vs. 213 mL/min ± 133 (P = 0.6) and 5.2 ± 3.3 vs. 4.2 ± 2.9 mmol/ (P = 0.5)]. Pressure-volume area (PVA) was significantly higher with VA-ECMO compared with ECMELLA (9567 ± 1733 vs. 6921 ± 5036 mmHg × mL/min × 10 -3, P = 0.014). Total diureses was found to be lower in VA-ECMO compared with ECMELLA [248 mL (179-930) vs. 506 mL (418-2190); P = 0.005]. CONCLUSIONS: In a porcine model of CS, we found lower PVA, with the ECMELLA configuration compared with VA-ECMO, indicating better cardiac energetics without compromising systemic perfusion.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Peter H.","Linde, Louise","Gregers, Emilie","Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Banke, Ann","Dahl, Jordi Sanchez","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Lassen, Jens Flensted","Povlsen, Amalie Ling","Larsen, Jeppe P.","Schmidt, Henrik","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-755487"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Frederiksen, Peter H."],"keyword":["Animals","Cardiogenic shock","Disease Models Animal","ECMELLA","Extracorporeal Membrane Oxygenation methods","Heart Assist Devices","Hemodynamics physiology","Impella","Pressure volume loops","Shock Cardiogenic therapy","Swine","VA ECMO"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"haemodynamic implications of va ecmo vs va ecmo plus impella cp for cardiogenic shock in a large animal model","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ehf2.14780","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-755487","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11287291","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85191153245","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38649295","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-9ec5f08b-0cef-46dd-b3ad-a784ad27067f"],"keyword":["Animals","Cardiogenic shock","Disease Models, Animal","ECMELLA","Extracorporeal Membrane Oxygenation/methods","Heart-Assist Devices","Hemodynamics/physiology","Impella","Pressure-volume loops","Shock, Cardiogenic/therapy","Swine","VA-ECMO"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F05684D599459DF0B9CD099883CB6F33"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/268641892/ESC_Heart_Failure_-_2024_-_Frederiksen_-_Haemodynamic_implications_of_VA_ECMO_vs_VA_ECMO_plus_Impella_CP_for_cardiogenic.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ehf2.14780","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter H.","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"85d6facd-93bf-44ee-a117-269fb26a52be","name":"Frederiksen, Peter H.","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-7980","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"lindepau","last":"Linde","locid":"4fc23628-00d4-466a-9e6e-269e23160481","name":"Linde, Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-7757-2571","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emilie","key":"gregerspau","last":"Gregers","name":"Gregers, Emilie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna L.J.","key":"udesenpau","last":"Udesen","locid":"f71f56f5-4f36-4de5-a7ae-e5e51f101a83","name":"Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","name_org":"Udesen, Nanna L.J.","orcid":"0000-0003-1542-3260","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole K.","key":"helgestadpau","last":"Helgestad","locid":"ab9f3165-500c-482b-9c2f-1879b3abedb3","name":"Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","name_org":"Helgestad, Ole K.","orcid":"0000-0003-3847-8758","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann","key":