ey":"holgersenpau","last":"Holgersen","name":"Holgersen, Mathias Geldermann","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5 4","first":"Thea Palsgaard","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Thea Palsgaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Stig Nikolaj Fasmer","key":"blombergpau","last":"Blomberg","name":"Blomberg, Stig Nikolaj Fasmer","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Bredevang","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lars Bredevang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"7df86a29-c6dc-4919-a9f9-6f5c23591e1d","name":"Mikkelsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-5187-7027","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 8 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"steinmetzpau","last":"Steinmetz","locid":"fc3ac4ad-1c4d-492e-bc3c-330a8af4e5be","name":"Steinmetz, Jacob","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Helle Collatz","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"b05bae82-5e32-4f10-980c-147b4af03d6a","name":"Christensen, Helle Collatz","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38100645"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/mej.0000000000001108","issn":["09699546","14735695"],"issn_org":["09699546"],"issue":"5","journal":"European Journal of Emergency Medicine","pages":"324-331","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins Ltd.","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Emergency Medicine","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85186735883"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","copenhagen university hospital - holbæk","danish air ambulance"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bf374a31-fe8a-45d4-9417-6bb28e740a94","ku-94184c12-cf4a-40d5-8060-83abd1edc14a","sdu-5cff08e6-292a-4e1d-87cc-c02ad1c66dc9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Prehospital interventions and outcomes in traumatic cardiac arrest : A population-based cohort study using the Danish Helicopter Emergency Medical Services data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-756090","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) survivors remaining comatose are often circulatory unstable with high mortality in the first days following resuscitation. Elevated lactate will reflect the severity and duration of hypoperfusion in cardiac arrest. Further, the severity of hypoperfusion could modify the effect on survival of different mean arterial blood pressure (MAP) targets. METHODS: In this sub-study of the BOX trial, adult successfully resuscitated comatose OHCA patients (n = 789) with a presumed cardiac cause were randomized to a MAP target of 63 mmHg vs. 77 mmHg. Patients were arbitrarily grouped in low-lactate: <25% of sample, medium-lactate: 25%-75%, and high >75 percentile according to blood lactate levels at hospital arrival as a surrogate of the severity of hypoperfusion. Invasive hemodynamic evaluations were performed using an arterial catheter and pulmonary artery catheter (PAC), and data from admission to 48 hours (h) were recorded. Logistic regression analysis evaluated whether lactate levels (as continuous and categorical) modify the effect of MAP targets on mortality at 365 days. RESULTS: The three lactate groups had initial lactate levels of low-lactate: <2.9 mmol/L, medium-lactate: 2.9-7.9 mmol/L, and high-lactate > 7.9 mmol/L. All patients were randomized to a 63 mmHg or 77 mmHg MAP target. The proportion of patients in the high-MAP target group was 100/201 (50%), 178/388 (46%), and 114/197 (58%) for low, medium, and high-lactate groups respectively. At admission, the high-lactate groups had a lower MAP compared to the medium-lactate (2.6 mmHg (95% CI: 0.1-5.0 mmHg, p = 0.02), and the low-lactate group, (3.6 mmHg (95% CI: 0.8-6.5 mmHg, p < 0.01). Accordingly, the vasoactive inotropic score was 79% (95%CI: 42%-124%%) higher with increasing initial lactate level (High-lactate vs. low-lactate) with the largest difference at 6 hours (110.6% (95%CI: 54.4%-187.2%) higher in high-lactate patients). No difference in the cardiac index or systemic vascular resistance was observed between lactate groups. The initial lactate level (continuous) modified the effect of the two MAP targets (p = 0.04). In the highest lactate group, the mortality was 100/197 (51%), and with an odds ratio (OR): 1.7 (95%CI: 0.9-3.0) if randomized to MAP 77 mmHg compared to MAP 63 mmHg. In the lowest lactate group, the mortality was 35/201(17%) and similar if randomized to a MAP target of 77 mmHg (OR: 1.1 (95% CI: 0.5-2.3)). CONCLUSION: Comatose OHCA patients with high initial lactate levels required more vasoactive drugs on the first two days of ICU admission to meet the blood pressure target and had a poorer prognosis. No indication that aiming for a higher MAP target is beneficial in patients with an initial high lactate level was found, however, given the post-hoc nature of this study, these results should be considered hypothesis-generating.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Beske, Rasmus P","Søndergaard, Frederik T","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Schmidt, Henrik","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Obling, Laust","Meyer, Martin A S","Mølstrøm, Simon","Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Højgaard, Henrik Frederiksen","Jeppesen, Karoline Korsholm","Sarkisian, Laura","Grand, Johannes","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-714385"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Beske, Rasmus P"],"keyword":["Invasive hemodynamics","Lactate","Noradrenaline","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Survival"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"treatment effects of blood pressure targets and hemodynamics according to initial blood lactate levels in comatose out of hospital cardiac arrest patients a sub study of the box trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2023.110007","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-714385","identifier":[{"id":"37863419","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85177743059","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-9841bc5c-b309-4e26-a0f9-9e5a7dd2f52a"],"keyword":["Invasive hemodynamics","Lactate","Noradrenaline","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","Targeted mean arterial blood pressure","Vaso-active drugs","survival"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DC3875C21888C0B5E1D9F6380B18FFA1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2023.110007","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/252814461/PIIS0300957223003222.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus P","key":"beskepau","last":"Beske","name":"Beske, Rasmus P","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik T","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","name":"Søndergaard, Frederik T","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laust","key":"oblingpau","last":"Obling","name":"Obling, Laust","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin A S","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Martin A S","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"mølstrømpau","last":"Mølstrøm","locid":"197d79e9-dd07-401b-90f8-1c26dc359db2","name":"Mølstrøm, Simon","orcid":"0000-0002-2778-8075","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matilde","key":"wintherjensenpau","last":"Winther-Jensen","name":"Winther-Jensen, Matilde","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Frederiksen","key":"højgaardpau","last":"Højgaard","locid":"98c46706-c074-48d3-a62c-d3fb83d08ab2","name":"Højgaard, Henrik Frederiksen","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karoline Korsholm","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"35431674-47f1-44be-a406-d01e49032afd","name":"Jeppesen, Karoline Korsholm","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"sarkisianpau","last":"Sarkisian","locid":"472392ba-c3e3-4a00-ae8e-9a24b7706ab3","name":"Sarkisian, Laura","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Johannes","key":"grandpau","last":"Grand","name":"Grand, Johannes","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"4025bf39-1de8-49eb-975c-cbc1a5f906ff","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37863419"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.resuscitation.2023.110007","issn":["03009572","18731570"],"issn_org":["03009572"],"journal":"Resuscitation","paperid":"110007","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Resuscitation","volume":"194"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85177743059"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-9841bc5c-b309-4e26-a0f9-9e5a7dd2f52a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Treatment effects of blood pressure targets and hemodynamics according to initial blood lactate levels in comatose out-of-hospital cardiac arrest patients - A sub study of the BOX trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-714385","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: In intensive care unit (ICU) patients with coma and other disorders of consciousness (DoC), outcome prediction is key to decision-making regarding prognostication, neurorehabilitation, and management of family expectations. Current prediction algorithms are largely based on chronic DoC, whereas multimodal data from acute DoC are scarce. Therefore, the Consciousness in Neurocritical Care Cohort Study Using Electroencephalography and Functional Magnetic Resonance Imaging (i.e. CONNECT-ME; ClinicalTrials.gov identifier: NCT02644265) investigates ICU patients with acute DoC due to traumatic and nontraumatic brain injuries, using electroencephalography (EEG) (resting-state and passive paradigms), functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI) (resting-state) and systematic clinical examinations. Methods: We previously presented results for a subset of patients (n = 87) concerning prediction of consciousness levels in the ICU. Now we report 3- and 12-month outcomes in an extended cohort (n = 123). Favorable outcome was defined as a modified Rankin Scale score ≤ 3, a cerebral performance category score ≤ 2, and a Glasgow Outcome Scale Extended score ≥ 4. EEG features included visual grading, automated spectral categorization, and support vector machine consciousness classifier. fMRI features included functional connectivity measures from six resting-state networks. Random forest and support vector machine were applied to EEG and fMRI features to predict outcomes. Here, random forest results are presented as areas under the curve (AUC) of receiver operating characteristic curves or accuracy. Cox proportional regression with in-hospital death as a competing risk was used to assess independent clinical predictors of time to favorable outcome. Results: Between April 2016 and July 2021, we enrolled 123 patients (mean age 51 years, 42% women). Of 82 (66%) ICU survivors, 3- and 12-month outcomes were available for 79 (96%) and 77 (94%), respectively. EEG features predicted both 3-month (AUC 0.79 [95% confidence interval (CI) 0.77–0.82]) and 12-month (AUC 0.74 [95% CI 0.71–0.77]) outcomes. fMRI features appeared to predict 3-month outcome (accuracy 0.69–0.78) both alone and when combined with some EEG features (accuracies 0.73–0.84) but not 12-month outcome (larger sample sizes needed). Independent clinical predictors of time to favorable outcome were younger age (hazard ratio [HR] 1.04 [95% CI 1.02–1.06]), traumatic brain injury (HR 1.94 [95% CI 1.04–3.61]), command-following abilities at admission (HR 2.70 [95% CI 1.40–5.23]), initial brain imaging without severe pathological findings (HR 2.42 [95% CI 1.12–5.22]), improving consciousness in the ICU (HR 5.76 [95% CI 2.41–15.51]), and favorable visual-graded EEG (HR 2.47 [95% CI 1.46–4.19]). Conclusions: Our results indicate that EEG and fMRI features and readily available clinical data predict short-term outcome of patients with acute DoC and that EEG also predicts 12-month outcome after ICU discharge.","author_count":30,"contributors":["Amiri, Moshgan","Raimondo, Federico","Fisher, Patrick M.","Cacic Hribljan, Melita","Sidaros, Annette","Othman, Marwan H.","Zibrandtsen, Ivan","Bergdal, Ove","Fabritius, Maria Louise","Hansen, Adam Espe","Hassager, Christian","Højgaard, Joan Lilja S.","Jensen, Helene Ravnholt","Knudsen, Niels Vendelbo","Laursen, Emilie Lund","Møller, Jacob E.","Nersesjan, Vardan","Nicolic, Miki","Sigurdsson, Sigurdur Thor","Sitt, Jacobo D.","Sølling, Christine","Welling, Karen Lise","Willumsen, Lisette M.","Hauerberg, John","Larsen, Vibeke Andrée","Fabricius, Martin","Knudsen, Gitte Moos","Kjærgaard, Jesper","Møller, Kirsten","Kondziella, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-732509"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Jülich Research Centre","Sorbonne University"],"keyword":["Coma","Consciousness","Electroencephalography","Functional magnetic resonance imaging","Intensive care unit"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multimodal prediction of 000000000003 and 000000000012 month outcomes in icu patients with acute disorders of consciousness","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12028-023-01816-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-732509","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10959792","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37697124","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85170360067","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d5439bec-3774-4da5-898d-3b046a3328f6"],"keyword":["Coma","Consciousness","Electroencephalography","Functional magnetic resonance imaging","Intensive care unit"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9BCD68EC0B6997D8853D7EBE2DCA3077"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12028-023-01816-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/387738479/s12028_023_01816_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"jülich research centre","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Jülich Research Centre","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"heinrich heine university düsseldor