null,"first":"Jannik","key":"helweglarsenjannikpau","last":"Helweg-Larsen","name":"Helweg-Larsen, Jannik","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Daniel","key":"faurholtjepsendanielpau","last":"Faurholt-Jepsen","locid":"789d8552-3f68-48cf-b78a-f616c0cd62b5","name":"Faurholt-Jepsen, Daniel","orcid":"0000-0001-8561-0155","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lauge","key":"østergaardlaugepau","last":"Østergaard","name":"Østergaard, Lauge","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Lars","key":"køberlarspau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Emil L.","key":"fosbølemilpau","last":"Fosbøl","locid":"3089319b-8ca3-4959-8e4a-072bdb702871","name":"Fosbøl, Emil","name_org":"Fosbøl, Emil L.","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38056547"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ahj.2023.11.018","issn":["00028703","10976744"],"issn_org":["00028703"],"journal":"American Heart Journal","pages":"80-93","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"American Heart Journal","volume":"268"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85182954962"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cacf9bf2-5b74-4406-8112-225fb28631cb","au-5efb066b-1eb7-4da8-8d0e-f400014a15f5","ku-347ad679-65d9-4237-b914-f561b47dbc5b","sdu-59691593-38d3-48b5-aa0e-0a16dd120ba1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"NatIonal Danish endocarditis stUdieS - Design and objectives of the NIDUS registry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-724341","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: The “Blood Pressure and Oxygenation Targets in Post Resuscitation Care” (BOX) trial investigated whether a low versus high blood pressure target, a restrictive versus liberal oxygenation target, and a shorter versus longer duration of device-based fever prevention in comatose patients could improve outcomes. No differences in rates of discharge from hospital with severe disability or 90-day mortality were found. However, long-term effects and potential interaction of the interventions are unknown. Accordingly, the objective of this study is to investigate both individual and combined effects of the interventions on 1-year mortality rates. Methods: The BOX trial was a randomized controlled two-center trial that assigned comatose resuscitated out-of-hospital cardiac arrest patients to the following three interventions at admission: A blood pressure target of either 63 mmHg or 77 mmHg; An arterial oxygenation target of 9–10 kPa or 13–14 kPa; Device-based fever prevention administered as an initial 24 h at 36 °C and then either 12 or 48 h at 37 °C; totaling 36 or 72 h of temperature control. Randomization occurred in parallel and simultaneously to all interventions. Patients were followed for the occurrence of death from all causes for 1 year. Analyzes were performed by Cox proportional models, and assessment of interactions was performed with the interventions stated as an interaction term. Results: Analysis for all three interventions included 789 patients. For the intervention of low compared to high blood pressure targets, 1-year mortality rates were 35% (138 of 396) and 36% (143 of 393), respectively, hazard ratio (HR) 0.92 (0.73–1.16) p = 0.47. For the restrictive compared to liberal oxygenation targets, 1-year mortality rates were 34% (135 of 394) and 37% (146 of 395), respectively, HR 0.92 (0.73–1.16) p = 0.46. For device-based fever prevention for a total of 36 compared to 72 h, 1-year mortality rates were 35% (139 of 393) and 36% (142 of 396), respectively, HR 0.98 (0.78–1.24) p = 0.89. There was no sign of interaction between the interventions, and accordingly, no combination of randomizations indicated differentiated treatment effects. Conclusions: There was no difference in 1-year mortality rates for a low compared to high blood pressure target, a liberal compared to restrictive oxygenation target, or a longer compared to shorter duration of device-based fever prevention after cardiac arrest. No combination of the interventions affected these findings. Trial registration ClinicalTrials.gov NCT03141099, Registered 30 April 2017.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Meyer, Martin A.S.","Hassager, Christian","Mølstrøm, Simon","Borregaard, Britt","Grand, Johannes","Nyholm, Benjamin","Obling, Laust E.R.","Beske, Rasmus P.","Meyer, Anna Sina P.","Bekker‑Jensen, Ditte","Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Jørgensen, Vibeke L.","Schmidt, Henrik","Møller, Jacob E.","Kjaergaard, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-089.29-716468"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Martin A.S."],"keyword":["Blood Pressure","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Oxygenation","Post resuscitation care","Temperature control"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"combined effects of targeted blood pressure oxygenation and duration of device based fever prevention after out of hospital cardiac arrest on 000000000001 year survival post hoc analysis of a randomized controlled trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-023-04794-y","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Open access funding provided by Copenhagen University. The BOX trial was supported by an unrestricted research grant from the Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF17OC0028706), and Professor Christian Hassager was supported by an unrestricted research grant from the Lundbeck Foundation (R186-2015-2132)."],"id":"S02-089.29-716468","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10785348","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85182210506","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38216985","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-9bb2c4be-9a4d-4f84-989f-2039582be553","sdu-b9a5ec57-78db-4bd1-97ca-cc845d26c0d5"],"keyword":["Blood pressure","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","Oxygenation","Post-resuscitation care","Temperature control"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-22C19610DAA6F5D634CAC2B7E447CC2E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/253612688/s13054-023-04794-y.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/380294271/s13054_023_04794_y.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-023-04794-y","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cl