{"abstract":"Many 3D hydrostratigraphic models of the subsurface are interpreted as deterministic models, where an experienced modeler combines relevant geophysical and geological information with background geological knowledge. Depending on the quality of the information from the input data, the interpretation phase will typically be accompanied by an estimated qualitative interpretation uncertainty. Given the qualitative nature of uncertainty, it is difficult to propagate the uncertainty to groundwater models. In this study, a stochastic-simulation-based methodology to characterize interpretation uncertainty within a manual-interpretation-based layer model is applied in a groundwater modeling setting. Three scenarios with different levels of interpretation uncertainty are generated, and three locations representing different geological structures are analyzed in the models. The impact of interpretation uncertainty on predictions of capture zone area and median travel time is compared to the impact of parameter uncertainty in the groundwater model. The main result is that in areas with thick and large aquifers and low geological uncertainty, the impact of interpretation uncertainty is negligible compared to the hydrogeological parameterization, while it may introduce a significant contribution in areas with thinner and smaller aquifers with high geologic uncertainty. The influence of the interpretation uncertainties is thus dependent on the geological setting as well as the confidence of the interpreter. In areas with thick aquifers, this study confirms existing evidence that if the conceptual model is well defined, interpretation uncertainties within the conceptual model have limited impact on groundwater model predictions.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Enemark, Trine","Madsen, Rasmus Bødker","Sonnenborg, Torben O","Andersen, Lærke Therese","Sandersen, Peter BE","Kidmose, Jacob","Møller, Ingelise","Hansen, Thomas Mejer","Jensen, Karsten Høgh","Høyer, Anne-Sophie"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-735247"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Nordic"],"corresponding_author":["Enemark, Trine"],"country":["Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incorporating interpretation uncertainties from deterministic 000000000003d hydrostratigraphic models in groundwater models","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/hess-28-505-2024","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-735247","identifier":[{"id":"85185881441","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-87be9e0c-2c13-4133-b697-c60387b5afa3","ku-5602f564-76b0-4590-a820-d9f3406d4b3a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-955C6A92C3FE363FE16E88E36EB27F04"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/hess-28-505-2024","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/389960719/Incorporating_interpretation_uncertainties_from_deterministic_3D_hydrostratigraphic_models_in_groundwater_models.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Geology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gl","key":"geological survey of denmark and greenland","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"geus geological survey of denmark and greenland","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-GEUS","l3nn":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","namevar":["Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-GEUS","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Trine","key":"enemarkpau","last":"Enemark","locid":"7d3a9c55-c88b-40f5-953a-2beaf60b040e","name":"Enemark, Trine","orcid":"0000-0002-3881-2739","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Bødker","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Rasmus Bødker","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben O","key":"sonnenborgpau","last":"Sonnenborg","name":"Sonnenborg, Torben O","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lærke Therese","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lærke Therese","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter BE","key":"sandersenpau","last":"Sandersen","name":"Sandersen, Peter BE","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"kidmosepau","last":"Kidmose","name":"Kidmose, Jacob","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingelise","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Ingelise","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Mejer","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5287a4df-485d-4328-ab19-1c04e64ccd96","name":"Hansen, Thomas Mejer","orcid":"0000-0003-4529-0112","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karsten Høgh","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"185c3ae4-342f-45a5-a650-182db1405d6f","name":"Jensen, Karsten Høgh","orcid":"0000-0003-4020-0050","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne-Sophie","key":"høyerpau","last":"Høyer","name":"Høyer, Anne-Sophie","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5194/hess-28-505-2024","issn":["10275606","16077938"],"issn_org":["10275606"],"issue":"3","journal":"Hydrology and Earth System Sciences","pages":"505-523","publisher":"Copernicus Publications","status":"p","title":"Hydrology and Earth System Sciences","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85185881441"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-87be9e0c-2c13-4133-b697-c60387b5afa3","ku-5602f564-76b0-4590-a820-d9f3406d4b3a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Incorporating interpretation uncertainties from deterministic 3D hydrostratigraphic models in groundwater models","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-735247","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"background The effects of temporary mechanical circulatory support with a microaxial flow pump on mortality among patients with ST-segment elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI) complicated by cardiogenic shock remains unclear. METHODS In an international, multicenter, randomized trial, we assigned patients with STEMI and cardiogenic shock to receive a microaxial flow pump (Impella CP) plus standard care or standard care alone. The primary end point was death from any cause at 180 days. A composite safety end point was severe bleeding, limb ischemia, hemolysis, device failure, or worsening aortic regurgitation. RESULTS A total of 360 patients underwent randomization, of whom 355 were included in the final analysis (179 in the microaxial-flow-pump group and 176 in the standard-care group). The median age of the patients was 67 years, and 79.2% were men. Death from any cause occurred in 82 of 179 patients (45.8%) in the microaxial-flow-pump group and in 103 of 176 patients (58.5%) in the standard-care group (hazard ratio, 0.74; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.55 to 0.99; P=0.04). A composite safety end-point event occurred in 43 patients (24.0%) in the microaxial-flow-pump group and in 11 (6.2%) in the standard-care group (relative risk, 4.74; 95% CI, 2.36 to 9.55). Renal-replacement therapy was administered to 75 patients (41.9%) in the microaxial-flow-pump group and to 47 patients (26.7%) in the standard-care group (relative risk, 1.98; 95% CI, 1.27 to 3.09). CONCLUSIONS The routine use of a microaxial flow pump with standard care in the treatment of patients with STEMI-related cardiogenic shock led to a lower risk of death from any cause at 180 days than standard care alone. The incidence of a composite of adverse events was higher with the use of the microaxial flow pump. (Funded by the Danish Heart Foundation and Abiomed; DanGer Shock ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT01633502.)","author_count":36,"contributors":["Møller, J. E.","Engstrøm, Thomas","Jensen, L. O.","Eiskjær, H.","Mangner, N.","Polzin, A.","Schulze, P. C.","Skurk, C.","Nordbeck, P.","Clemmensen, P.","Panoulas, V.","Zimmer, S.","Schäfer, A.","Werner, N.","Frydland, M.","Holmvang, Lene","Kjærgaard, J.","Sørensen, R.","Lønborg, J.","Lindholm, M. G.","Udesen, N. L.J.","Junker, A.","Schmidt, H.","Terkelsen, C. J.","Christensen, S.","Christiansen, E. H.","Linke, A.","Woitek, F. J.","Westenfeld, R.","Möbius-Winkler, S.","Wachtell, K.","Ravn, H. B.","Lassen, J. F.","Boesgaard, S.","Gerke, O.","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S03-099.97-735085"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["DanGer Shock investigators","for the DanGer Shock Investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University","Deutsches Herzzentrum Berlin","Dresden University of Technology","Friedrich Schiller University Jena","Hannover Medical School","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Royal Brompton and Harefield NHS Foundation Trust","University Hospital Bonn","University of Bonn","University of Würzburg"],"keyword":["Aged","Assisted Circulation adverse effects","Female","Heart Assist Devices adverse effects","Humans","Incidence","Male","ST Elevation Myocardial Infarction complications","Shock Cardiogenic etiology","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Heart Center Dresden"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microaxial flow pump or standard care in infarct related cardiogenic 