y of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","collaboration for research in intensive care","copenhagen university hospital - holbæk"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-16cff872-d159-4667-9c85-f957df9c0e3a","au-49bcfb67-0c0d-4f23-a346-fc1015fabaed","ku-357781f5-bd54-4f4e-b7e2-66e29a4be965","sdu-dded98f3-12ae-4b02-a0b5-73bef0734931"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Long-term effects of restriction of intravenous fluid in adult ICU patients with septic shock","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-095.92-813304","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The 12-item version of the Kansas City Cardiomyopathy Questionnaire (KCCQ-12) was originally developed for patients with heart failure but has been used and tested among patients with severe aortic stenosis (AS) who underwent transcatheter aortic valve implantation. Whether the instrument is suitable for patients with AS who underwent surgical aortic valve replacement (SAVR) is currently unknown. Thus, we aimed to investigate the psychometric properties of the KCCQ-12 before and after SAVR among patients with severe AS. We conducted a prospective cohort of 184 patients with AS who completed the KCCQ-12 and the EuroQol 5 Dimension 5 Levels before and 4 weeks after surgery. Construct validity was investigated with hypothesis testing and an analysis of Spearman's correlation between the two instruments. Structural validity was investigated with explorative and confirmatory factor analyses and reliability with Cronbach's α. All analyses were conducted on data from the two time points (preoperatively and four weeks after surgery). The hypothesis testing revealed how the New York Heart Association class was significantly correlated with the preoperative KCCQ-12 total score (higher New York Heart Association class, worse score). A longer length of hospital stay and living alone were significantly associated with poorer postoperative KCCQ-12 total score. KCCQ-12 and EuroQol 5 Dimension 5 Levels were moderately correlated in most domains/the total score/Visual Analogue Scale score. Principal component analyses revealed two 3-factor structures. The confirmatory factor analyses did not support the original model at any time point. Cronbach's α ranged from 0.22 to 0.84 in three preoperative factors and from 0.39 to 0.76 in the postoperative factors. The total Cronbach's α was 0.83 for the suggested preoperative 3-factor model and 0.83 for the postoperative model. In conclusion, the Danish version of the KCCQ-12 tested in a population of patients with AS who underwent SAVR appears to have acceptable construct validity, whereas structural validity cannot be confirmed for the original four-factor model. Overall reliability is good.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Borregaard, Britt","Bruvik, Sofie Moesgaard","Dahl, Jordi Sanchez","Ekholm, Ola","Bekker-Jensen, Ditte","Sibilitz, Kirstine Lærum","Zwisler, Ann Dorthe Olsen","Lauck, Sandra B","Pedersen, Susanne S.","Norekvål, Tone","Riber, Lars","Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-722907"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Borregaard, Britt"],"country":["Canada","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Haukeland University Hospital","St. Paul's Hospital","University of British Columbia (UBC)"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"psychometric properties of the kansas city cardiomyopathy questionnaire in a surgical population of patients with aortic valve stenosis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.amjcard.2023.09.068","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-722907","identifier":[{"id":"85174976197","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37898098","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-1152e356-eb05-4907-950c-709387e43182"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C79B8E2BC09A9A8D9760AFD5B5E71C14"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/245487948/1_s2.0_S0002914923010627_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.amjcard.2023.09.068","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiac, thoracic, and Vascular surgery (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"st paul s hospital","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"St. Paul's Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"university of british columbia","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of British Columbia (UBC)","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"no","key":"haukeland university hospital","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Haukeland University Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Britt","key":"borregaardpau","last":"Borregaard","locid":"ca3a0f85-e4e4-42dc-98f0-a7ddfe619020","name":"Borregaard, Britt","orcid":"0000-0003-2702-0231","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie Moesgaard","key":"bruvikpau","last":"Bruvik","locid":"60983f8a-f7c0-49b3-8e69-c172c904fd5d","name":"Bruvik, Sofie Moesgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jordi","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"fa82ce60-e408-4c0f-b013-151f87c6998c","name":"Dahl, Jordi Sanchez","name_org":"Dahl, Jordi","orcid":"0000-0002-8345-204X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ola","key":"ekholmpau","last":"Ekholm","locid":"b59d640e-8087-46d7-8284-5a45e6ebd03f","name":"Ekholm, Ola","orcid":"0000-0002-5563-7098","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte","key":"bekkerjensenpau","last":"Bekker-Jensen","locid":"2fba1c68-3012-4341-985b-1bef26ea4da6","name":"Bekker-Jensen, Ditte","orcid":"0000-0002-0145-6128","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirstine Lærum","key":"sibilitzpau","last":"Sibilitz","name":"Sibilitz, Kirstine Lærum","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann Dorthe","key":"zwislerpau","last":"Zwisler","locid":"6e2c85c0-d456-45f2-a017-7942ea7eb12a","name":"Zwisler, Ann Dorthe Olsen","name_org":"Zwisler, Ann Dorthe","orcid":"0000-0002-9241-2090","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandra B","key":"lauckpau","last":"Lauck","name":"Lauck, Sandra B","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Susanne S","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"8ee710a4-b477-4b42-acf0-acf2bd8ddde2","name":"Pedersen, Susanne S.","name_org":"Pedersen, Susanne S","orcid":"0000-0001-8055-3251","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Tone","key":"norekvålpau","last":"Norekvål","name":"Norekvål, Tone","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars P Schødt","key":"riberpau","last":"Riber","locid":"607e34a6-2b96-4466-ad5f-48b2c188f589","name":"Riber, Lars","name_org":"Riber, Lars P Schødt","orcid":"0000-0001-6898-2715","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37898098"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.amjcard.2023.09.068","issn":["00029149","18791913"],"issn_org":["00029149"],"journal":"American Journal of Cardiology","pages":"165-172","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Cardiology","title_org":"The American Journal of Cardiology","volume":"209"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174976197"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-1152e356-eb05-4907-950c-709387e43182"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Psychometric Properties of the Kansas City Cardiomyopathy Questionnaire in a Surgical Population of Patients With Aortic Valve Stenosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-722907","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Acute kidney injury (AKI) represents a common and serious complication to out-of-hospital cardiac arrest. The importance of post-resuscitation care targets for blood pressure and oxygenation for the development of AKI is unknown. METHODS: This is a substudy of a randomized 2-by-2 factorial trial, in which 789 comatose adult patients who had out-of-hospital cardiac arrest with presumed cardiac cause and sustained return of spontaneous circulation were randomly assigned to a target mean arterial blood pressure of either 63 or 77 mm Hg. Patients were simultaneously randomly assigned to either a restrictive oxygen target of a partial pressure of arterial oxygen (Pao2) of 9 to 10 kPa or a liberal oxygenation target of a Pao2 of 13 to 14 kPa. The primary outcome for this study was AKI according to KDIGO (Kidney Disease: Improving Global Outcomes) classification in patients surviving at least 48 hours (N=759). Adjusted logistic regression was performed for patients allocated to high blood pressure and liberal oxygen target as reference. RESULTS: The main population characteristics at admission were: age, 64 (54-73) years; 80% male; 90% shockable rhythm; and time to return of spontaneous circulation, 18 (12-26) minutes. Patients allocated to a low blood pressure and liberal oxygen target had an increased risk of developing AKI compared with patients with high blood pressure and liberal oxygen target (84/193 [44%] versus 56/187 [30%]; adjusted odds ratio, 1.87 [95% CI, 1.21-2.89]). Multinomial logistic regression revealed that the increased risk of AKI was only related to mild-stage AKI (KDIGO stage 1). There was no difference in risk of AKI in the other groups. Plasma creatinine remained high during hospitalization in the low blood pressure and liberal oxygen target group but did not differ between groups at 6- and 12-month follow-up. CONCLUSIONS: In comatose patients who had been resuscitated after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest, patients allocated to a combination of a low mean arterial blood pressure and a liberal oxygen target had a significantly increased risk of mild-stage AKI. No difference was found in terms of more severe AKI stages or other kidney-related adverse outcomes, and creatinine had normalized at 1 year after discharge. REGISTRATION: URL: https://www.clinicaltrials.gov; Unique identifier: NCT03141099.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Sebastian Buhl","Jeppesen, Karoline Korsholm","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Hassager, Christian","Schmidt, Henrik","Mølstrøm, Simon","Beske, Rasmus Paulin","Grand, Johannes","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Meyer, Martin Abild Stengaard","Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"cuid":["S02-088.24-716460"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"keyword":["Acute kidney injury","Blood Pressure","Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Oxygen Inhalation Therapy","Post cardiac arrest syndrome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"blood pressure and oxygen targets on kidney injury after cardiac arrest","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85178668112","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Part of Dr Hassager’s salary was paid by a grant from the Lundbeck Foundation (R186-2015-2132). Acknowledgments The authors express their sincere gratitude to the patients, relatives, and staff of the participating sites. In particular, the nursing staff of the cardiac intensive care units at both sites committed themselves to diligent adherence to the trial protocol. J.N. Larsen is acknowledged for the development of the system for proxy consent, significantly reducing the time to randomization in the trial. Sources of Funding The NovoNordisk Foundation funded the trial (NNF17OC0028706). Part of Dr Hassager's salary was paid by a grant from the Lundbeck Foundation (R186- 2015-2132)."],"id":"S02-088.24-716460","identifier":[{"id":"37791480","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85178668112","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9294100f-1cab-40e0-89cb-616965fa88f6","sdu-cc428b19-6d17-4856-a8e9-ab391760f17e"],"keyword":["acute kidney injury","blood pressure","cardiopulmonary resuscitation","oxygen inhalation therapy","post-cardiac arrest syndrome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-06F1A9614366DD1A01DEF2ED4364D982"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Buhl","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ab6fae27-1823-419c-94e5-9fd43df69e74","name":"Rasmussen, Sebastian Buhl","orcid":"0000-0002-3990-2197","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karoline Korsholm","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"35431674-47f1-44be-a406-d01e49032afd","name":"Jeppesen, Karoline Korsholm","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","name":"Kjaergaard, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"mølstrømpau","last":"Mølstrøm","locid":"197d79e9-dd07-401b-90f8-1c26dc359db2","name":"Mølstrøm, Simon","orcid":"0000-0002-2778-8075","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Paulin","key":"beskepau","last":"Beske","name":"Beske, Rasmus Paulin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Johannes","key":"grandpau","last":"Grand","name":"Grand, Johannes","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Berg","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"25de7650-3dc1-4594-b758-9c36f6de6306","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","orcid":"0000-0003-4702-5195","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Matilde","key":"wintherjensenpau","last":"Winther-Jensen","name":"Winther-Jensen, Matilde","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Abild Stengaard","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Martin Abild Stengaard","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37791480"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/circulationaha.123.066012","issn":["00097322","15244539"],"issn_org":["00097322"],"issue":"23","journal":"Circulation","pages":"1860-1869","publisher":"American Heart Association","status":"p","title":"Circulation","volume":"148"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85178668112"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9294100f-1cab-40e0-89cb-616965fa88f6","sdu-cc428b19-6d17-4856-a8e9-ab391760f17e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Blood Pressure and Oxygen Targets on Kidney Injury After Cardiac Arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.24-716460","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Diverting loop ileostomy has become routine in low anterior resection (LAR) for rectal cancer. The optimal time for stoma reversal is controversial. The aim of the present study was to compare the results after planned early (within 8-12 days) versus late (> 3 months) stoma reversal. The primary outcomes were morbidity and mortality, as measured by the Comprehensive Complication Index (CCI) within 30 days after stoma reversal, and the secondary outcomes were morbidity and mortality within 90 days after LAR. This was a multicentre trial including all patients scheduled for anterior low resection for rectal cancer with curative intent. Inclusion period was from April 2011 to December 2018. All patients were randomized 1:1 prior to surgery. Among 257 consecutive and eligible patients, a total of 214 patients were randomized: 107 patients to early stoma reversal and 107 to late reversal. A total of 68 patients were excluded for various reasons, and 146 patients completed the study, with 77 in the early reversal group and 69 in the late reversal group. The patients were asked to complete the Gastrointestinal Quality of Life Index before surgery (baseline) and at 6 and 12 months after LAR. Ostomy-related complications were evaluated by dedicated ostomy staff using the validated DET score. ClinicalTrials Identifier: NCT01865071. Fifty-three patients (69%) in the early reversal group and 60 patients (87%) in the late reversal group received the intended treatment. There were no significant differences in CCI within 90 days after index surgery with the LAR and within 30 days after stoma reversal between the two groups. There were no differences in patient-reported quality of life but significantly more stoma-related complications in the late reversal group. A total of 5 patients experienced anastomotic leakage (AL) after stoma reversal, 4 in the early reversal group and one in the late reversal group. Early and late stoma reversal showed similar outcomes in terms of overall complications and quality of life. The risk of developing anastomotic leakage after early ostomy reversal is a concern.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Ellebæk, Mark Bremholm","Perdawood, Sharaf Karim","Jensen, Signe Steenstrup","Khalaf, Sardar","Kundal, Jette","Möller, Sören","Bang, Jacob Christian","Overgaard Støvring, Jens","Qvist, Niels"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-671851"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ellebæk, Mark Bremholm"],"keyword":["Anastomosis Surgical","Anastomotic leak","Humans","Ileostomy adverse effects","Postoperative Complications etiology","Quality of Life","Rectal Neoplasms surgery","Retrospective Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"early versus late reversal of diverting loop ileostomy in rectal cancer surgery a multicentre randomized controlled trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-33006-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-671851","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10085999","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37037856","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85152100678","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-bfc87d21-308b-4768-b339-7e5ec32ce8b9"],"keyword":["Anastomosis, Surgical","Anastomotic Leak","Humans","Ileostomy/adverse effects","Postoperative Complications/etiology","Quality of Life","Rectal Neoplasms/surgery","Retrospective Studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3B1C6AC3A0661F8EE83E6153A2B37A43"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/227392181/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-33006-4","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Næstved-Slagelse-Ringsted Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark Bremholm","key":"ellebækpau","last":"Ellebæk","locid":"80a5416e-11fe-4eb8-97de-0d1b3e412452","name":"Ellebæk, Mark Bremholm","orcid":"0000-0001-6550-7505","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sharaf Karim","key":"perdawoodpau","last":"Perdawood","name":"Perdawood, Sharaf Karim","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe","key":"steenstruppau","last":"Steenstrup","locid":"be68fdf8-9295-46e9-a160-9bf95cf5ee3d","name":"Jensen, Signe Steenstrup","name_org":"Steenstrup, Signe","orcid":"0000-0003-1563-3778","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sardar","key":"khalafpau","last":"Khalaf","locid":"01096652-f84c-4b8e-84e7-68cfde8ae60c","name":"Khalaf, Sardar","orcid":"0009-0008-4358-4663","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jette","key":"kundalpau","last":"Kundal","name":"Kundal, Jette","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sören","key":"möllerpau","last":"Möller","locid":"905018dc-c6c4-4a79-b50d-d0c08618e77a","name":"Möller, Sören","orcid":"0000-0003-0858-4269","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Christian","key":"bangpau","last":"Bang","locid":"86ec2e26-c79d-4b32-b312-e431240cb020","name":"Bang, Jacob Christian","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"støvringpau","last":"Støvring","locid":"b46eda94-c2bc-4790-beb4-e84249a230a4","name":"Overgaard Støvring, Jens","name_org":"Støvring, Jens","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"qvistpau","last":"Qvist","locid":"1e82ad79-62c0-4d35-bb84-5d027f77dedd","name":"Qvist, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-1113-195X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37037856"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-023-33006-4","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","pages":"5818","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85152100678"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-bfc87d21-308b-4768-b339-7e5ec32ce8b9"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Early versus late reversal of diverting loop ileostomy in rectal cancer surgery : a multicentre randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-671851","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Study objective The objective was to assess the effect of ongoing angiotensin receptor-neprilysin inhibitor(ARNI) on the effect of the sodium glucose cotransporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitor empagliflozin on left ventricular (LV) size and function in patients with heart failure and reduced ejection fraction(HFrEF). Design Post hoc analysis of the Empire HF trial, an investigator-initiated, double-blind, randomized controlled trial. Participants 190 patients with HFrEF with New York Heart association class I-III symptoms with an ejection fraction of 40 % or below. Patients were stratified according to ongoing ARNI treatment at baseline. Intervention Empagliflozin 10 mg daily or placebo for 12 weeks. Echocardiography at baseline and follow-up. Main outcome measures Left ventricular end-systolic volume index (LVESVI), end-diastolic volume index (LVEDVI), left atrial volume index (LAVI), left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF). Results A total of 58 patients (31 %) received ARNI at baseline. Compared to with placebo, empagliflozin reduced the LVESVI ([−6.2 (−14.1 to 1.6); p = 0.12] and [−3.3 (−8.2 to 1.6); p = 0.19], interaction P = 0.49), LVEDVI ([−11.2 (−21.2 to −1.2); p = 0.03] and [−2.9 (−8.7 to 2.9); p = 0.32], interaction P = 0.13), and LAVI ([−3.9 (−9.1 to 1.2); p = 0.14] and. [−1.8 (−4.4 to 0.7); p = 0.16], respectively, interaction P = 0.9) in patients treated with and without ARNI at baseline, respectively. No treatment-by-ARNI subgroup interaction were found. Unaffected by baseline ARNI treatment, empagliflozin did not improve LVEF. Conclusion The effect of empagliflozin on cardiac structure and function compared to placebo was not affected by background treatment with ARNI.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Larsen, Julie Hempel","Omar, Massar","Jensen, Jesper","Andersen, Camilla Fuchs","Kistrup, Caroline Michaela","Poulsen, Mikael Kjær","Videbæk, Lars","Gustafsson, Finn","Køber, Lars","Schou, Morten","Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"cuid":["S02-099.93-692301"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Julie Hempel"],"keyword":["Angiotensin receptor neprilysin inhibitor","Heart failure","Sacubitril","Valsartan"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of angiotensin receptor neprilysin inhibition on the efficacy of empagliflozin on cardiac structure and function in patients with chronic heart failure and a reduced ejection fraction the empire hf trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ahjo.2023.100264","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.93-692301","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10946004","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85153867896","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38510180","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b55cde49-7bf1-4122-bd1f-92344200a8a9","sdu-6a7aee74-5c9f-493e-8ae4-8936d17673d4"],"keyword":["Angiotensin Receptor-Neprilysin Inhibitor","Heart failure","Sacubitril","Sodium-glucose cotransport 2 inhibitor","Valsartan"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7FB9A9DE2421BFCAA75877CF60869B4F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/370115344/1_s2.0_S2666602223000162_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ahjo.2023.100264","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/237887643/1_s2.0_S2666602223000162_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Herlev og Gentofte Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, Section for Medicine and Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Julie Hempel","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"750e6fe3-4c0c-4940-bfa9-7159856181ef","name":"Larsen, Julie Hempel","orcid":"0000-0002-2326-5736","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Massar","key":"omarpau","last":"Omar","locid":"3a6641e9-a451-482c-a139-b60841705f94","name":"Omar, Massar","orcid":"0000-0002-9634-3889","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 3","first":"Camilla Fuchs","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3ad58855-eaf8-45aa-a5a9-7ae16be4a2b6","name":"Andersen, Camilla","name_org":"Andersen, Camilla Fuchs","orcid":"0000-0002-6659-154X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Caroline Michaela","key":"kistruppau","last":"Kistrup","name":"Kistrup, Caroline Michaela","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikael Kjær","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"a8da3614-e99d-403f-933f-f5dfab3976af","name":"Poulsen, Mikael Kjær","orcid":"0000-0003-4051-7197","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"videbækpau","last":"Videbæk","locid":"c0abdf18-4e26-411a-99c3-de3cbe029dee","name":"Videbæk, Lars","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 3","first":"Finn","key":"gustafssonpau","last":"Gustafsson","locid":"6716eef1-891b-4209-a823-e96e765b9433","name":"Gustafsson, Finn","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 3","first":"Lars","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 3","first":"Morten","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"48fa6ec9-1941-4566-b931-14b0cc8cbae3","name":"Schou, Morten","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38510180"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ahjo.2023.100264","issn":["26666022"],"journal":"American Heart Journal Plus: Cardiology Research and Practice","paperid":"100264","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"American Heart Journal Plus: Cardiology Research and Practice","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85153867896"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b55cde49-7bf1-4122-bd1f-92344200a8a9","sdu-6a7aee74-5c9f-493e-8ae4-8936d17673d4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Influence of angiotensin receptor-neprilysin inhibition on the efficacy of Empagliflozin on cardiac structure and function in patients with chronic heart failure and a reduced ejection fraction: The Empire HF trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.93-692301","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Aims: It remains unknown whether the consistently observed increase in haematocrit with sodium–glucose cotransporter 2 inhibitors is caused by diuresis-associated haemoconcentration or increased erythropoiesis. We aimed to investigate the early effect of empagliflozin on erythropoiesis and iron metabolism in patients with heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (HFrEF). Methods and results: The Empire HF was a double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled trial. Patients with a left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) ≤40%, New York Heart Association (NYHA) class I–III symptoms, and on stable guideline-directed HFrEF therapy were randomly assigned (1:1) to empagliflozin or matching placebo once daily for 12 weeks. Exploratory outcomes reflecting changes in erythropoiesis and iron metabolism were analysed. In total, 190 patients were randomized. Baseline characteristics were well-balanced between the groups (age: mean 64 [± 11] years; male: 85%; LVEF: mean 29 [± 8)%; NYHA class II: 78%; type 2 diabetes: 13%; anaemia: 28%; chronic kidney disease: 13%). In this post hoc analysis, erythropoietin was increased with empagliflozin compared to placebo from baseline to 12 weeks (adjusted mean difference 2.6 IU/L, 95% confidence interval [CI] 0.8–4.4; p = 0.0046). Moreover, hepcidin was reduced (adjusted ratio of change 0.76, 95% CI 0.59–0.97; p = 0.031), with no change observed for erythroferrone (adjusted ratio of change 1.17, 95% CI 0.86–1.60; p = 0.31) compared to placebo. No significant treatment-by-subgroup interactions were observed regarding baseline type 2 diabetes, anaemia, or chronic kidney disease (pinteraction >0.05). Conclusion: These findings suggest that empagliflozin increases erythropoiesis and augments early iron utilization in patients with HFrEF. These mechanisms may contribute to the cardioprotective properties of empagliflozin.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Fuchs Andersen, Camilla","Omar, Massar","Glenthøj, Andreas","El Fassi, Daniel","Møller, Holger Jon","Lindholm Kurtzhals, Jørgen A.","Styrishave, Bjarne","Kistorp, Caroline","Tuxen, Christian","Poulsen, Mikael K.","Faber, Jens","Køber, Lars","Gustafsson, Finn","Møller, Jacob E.","Schou, Morten","Jensen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S03-097.25-026117"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Jesper"],"keyword":["Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 drug therapy","Erythropoiesis","Heart failure","Humans","Male","Pharmacotherapy","Renal Insufficiency Chronic","SGLT2 inhibitor","Sodium Glucose Transporter 2 Inhibitors therapeutic use","Stroke Volume","Ventricular Dysfunction Left drug therapy","Ventricular Function Left"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of empagliflozin on erythropoiesis in heart failure data from the empire hf trial","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ejhf.2735","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-097.25-026117","identifier":[{"id":"85144130941","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36377106","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b8d92208-f2ea-40df-932f-0592130e1987","ku-6eb15839-5331-4074-b606-72fbb5630072","sdu-64291af6-38e0-48f6-a259-561a698c3488"],"keyword":["Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/drug therapy","Erythropoiesis","Heart failure","Humans","Male","Pharmacotherapy","Renal Insufficiency, Chronic","SGLT2 inhibitor","Sodium-Glucose Transporter 2 Inhibitors/therapeutic use","Stroke Volume","Ventricular Dysfunction, Left/drug therapy","Ventricular Function, Left"],"lang":"English","level":"Scien