orresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Berg","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"25de7650-3dc1-4594-b758-9c36f6de6306","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","orcid":"0000-0003-4702-5195","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35925990"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0272279","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"8","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0272279","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135426530"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0f0b5320-ce4c-4bc5-8d69-ca32a2e728f4","sdu-4437a510-e04e-43d3-9543-6554dc396fa5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Vasoactive pharmacological management according to SCAI class in patients with acute myocardial infarction and cardiogenic shock","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.18-040173","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Introduction:Despite advances in treatment of patients with cardiogenic shock following acute myocardial infarction (AMICS) in-hospital mortality remains around 50%. Outcome varies among patient subsets and the elderly often have a poor a priori prognosis. We sought to investigate outcome among elderly AMICS patients referred to evaluation and treatment at a tertiary university hospital.Methods:Current analysis was based on the RETROSHOCK registry comprising consecutive AMICS patients admitted to tertiary care. Patients in the registry were individually identified and validated.Results:Of 1,716 admitted patients, 496 (28.9%) patients were ≥75 years old. Older patients were less likely to be admitted directly to a tertiary centre (59.4% vs. 69.9%, P = 0.003), receive mechanical support devices (i.e., Impella® (8.9% vs. 15.0%, P = 0.003), and undergo revascularization attempt (76.8% vs. 90.2%, P < 0.001). Thirty-day survivors ≥75 years were characterized by having higher left ventricular ejection fraction (30.2% ± 12.5% vs. 26.5% ± 11.8%, P = 0.004) and lower arterial lactate (3.2[2.2-5.2] mmol/L vs. 5.5[3.3-8.2] mmol/L, P < 0.001) at admission. In a multivariable analysis of patients ≥75 years, higher age (HR 1.09, 95% CI 1.05-1.14, P < 0.001), higher heart rate (HR 1.01, 95% CI 1.001-1.014, P = 0.03), and higher lactate (HR 1.11, 95% CI 1.07-1.16, P < 0.001) at admission were associated with an increased risk of 30-day mortality.Conclusion:Among patients ≥75 years with AMICS referred for tertiary specialized treatment, 30-day mortality was 73.4%. Survivors were characterized by lower arterial lactate and heart rate at admission.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Ratcovich, Hanna Louise","Josiassen, Jakob","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Linde, Louise","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Joshi, Francis R.","Engstrøm, Thomas","Schmidt, Henrik","Hassager, Christian","Møller, Jacob E.","Holmvang, Lene"],"cuid":["S02-092.10-040584"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ratcovich, Hanna Louise"],"keyword":["Acute coronary syndrome","Age Factors","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Cardiogenic shock","Cohort Studies","Denmark","Elderly","Female","Hospital Mortality","Hospitalization","Humans","Lactic Acid blood","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction complications","Registries","Risk Factors","Shock Cardiogenic etiology","Stroke Volume","Survival Rate","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"outcome in elderly patients with cardiogenic shock complicating acute myocardial infarction","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85125552958","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-092.10-040584","identifier":[{"id":"85125552958","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34265831","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1a671c56-68b3-444d-9945-7923f7c964c2","sdu-d914cbc4-bc14-4157-8e5f-bfc0d6abb3b9"],"keyword":["Acute coronary syndrome","Age Factors","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Cohort Studies","Denmark","Female","Hospital Mortality","Hospitalization","Humans","Lactic Acid/blood","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction/complications","Registries","Risk Factors","Shock, Cardiogenic/etiology","Stroke Volume","Survival Rate","Treatment Outcome","cardiogenic shock","elderly","tertiary care"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E97A8B7E8B7A43C2C587D8AFE795C388"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Hanna Louise","key":"ratcovichpau","last":"Ratcovich","name":"Ratcovich, Hanna Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jakob","key":"josiassenpau","last":"Josiassen","locid":"3bad0c12-b148-41c0-8a21-4ab4911c27e9","name":"Josiassen, Jakob","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole Kristian Lerche","key":"helgestadpau","last":"Helgestad","locid":"ab9f3165-500c-482b-9c2f-1879b3abedb3","name":"Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","orcid":"0000-0003-3847-8758","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"lindepau","last":"Linde","locid":"4fc23628-00d4-466a-9e6e-269e23160481","name":"Linde, Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-7757-2571","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette Okkels","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hanne Berg","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"3049e7b7-0f18-413b-88ab-a3d77ebc079b","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Francis R.","key":"joshipau","last":"Joshi","name":"Joshi, Francis R.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"engstrømpau","last":"Engstrøm","locid":"77ddb69e-092a-4c53-bbf0-409cdd3d12f7","name":"Engstrøm, Thomas","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob E.","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","name_org":"Møller, Jacob E.","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene","key":"holmvangpau","last":"Holmvang","locid":"54b8ef01-f8ed-4c49-a126-2109e2fd351f","name":"Holmvang, Lene","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34265831"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/shk.0000000000001837","issn":["10732322","15400514"],"issn_org":["10732322"],"issue":"3","journal":"Shock","pages":"327-335","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Shock","title_org":"Shock (Augusta, Ga.)","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85125552958"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1a671c56-68b3-444d-9945-7923f7c964c2","sdu-d914cbc4-bc14-4157-8e5f-bfc0d6abb3b9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Outcome in Elderly Patients With Cardiogenic Shock Complicating Acute Myocardial Infarction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.10-040584","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Evidence to support the choice of blood-pressure targets for the treatment of comatose survivors of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest who are receiving intensive care is limited. METHODS: In a double-blind, randomized trial with a 2-by-2 factorial design, we evaluated a mean arterial blood-pressure target of 63 mm Hg as compared with 77 mm Hg in comatose adults who had been resuscitated after an out-of-hospital cardiac arrest of presumed cardiac cause; patients were also assigned to one of two oxygen targets (reported separately). The primary outcome was a composite of death from any cause or hospital discharge with a Cerebral Performance Category (CPC) of 3 or 4 within 90 days (range, 0 to 5, with higher categories indicating more severe disability; a category of 3 or 4 indicates severe disability or coma). Secondary outcomes included neuron-specific enolase levels at 48 hours, death from any cause, scores on the Montreal Cognitive Assessment (range, 0 to 30, with higher scores indicating better cognitive ability) and the modified Rankin scale (range, 0 to 6, with higher scores indicating greater disability) at 3 months, and the CPC at 3 months. RESULTS: A total of 789 patients were included in the analysis (393 in the high-target group and 396 in the low-target group). A primary-outcome event occurred in 133 patients (34%) in the high-target group and in 127 patients (32%) in the low-target group (hazard ratio, 1.08; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.84 to 1.37; P = 0.56). At 90 days, 122 patients (31%) in the high-target group and 114 patients (29%) in the low-target group had died (hazard ratio, 1.13; 95% CI, 0.88 to 1.46). The median CPC was 1 (interquartile range, 1 to 5) in both the high-target group and the low-target group; the corresponding median modified Rankin scale scores were 1 (interquartile range, 0 to 6) and 1 (interquartile range, 0 to 6), and the corresponding median Montreal Cognitive Assessment scores were 27 (interquartile range, 24 to 29) and 26 (interquartile range, 24 to 29). The median neuron-specific enolase level at 48 hours was also similar in the two groups. The percentages of patients with adverse events did not differ significantly between the groups. CONCLUSIONS: Targeting a mean arterial blood pressure of 77 mm Hg or 63 mm Hg in patients who had been resuscitated from cardiac arrest did not result in significantly different percentages of patients dying or having severe disability or coma. (Funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation; BOX ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT03141099.).","author_count":27,"contributors":["Kjaergaard, Jesper","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Schmidt, Henrik","Grand, Johannes","Mølstrøm, Simon","Borregaard, Britt","Venø, Søren","Sarkisian, Laura","Mamaev, Dmitry","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Nyholm, Benjamin","Høfsten, Dan E.","Josiassen, Jakob","Thomsen, Jakob H.","Thune, Jens J.","Obling, Laust E.R.","Lindholm, Matias G.","Frydland, Martin","Meyer, Martin A.S.","Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Beske, Rasmus P.","Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth","Wiberg, Sebastian","Boesgaard, Søren","Madsen, Søren A.","Jørgensen, Vibeke L.","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-099.68-045694"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Kjaergaard, Jesper"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"blood pressure targets in comatose survivors of cardiac arrest","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1056/NEJMoa2208687","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.68-045694","identifier":[{"id":"85140002929","type":"scopus