istribution in Patients With Chronic Heart Failure and Reduced Ejection Fraction : An Analysis From the Empire HF Randomized Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.94-041281","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Hyposalivation and xerostomia (dry mouth), are the leading site-effects to treatment of head and neck cancer. Currently, there are no effective therapies to alleviate radiation-induced hyposalivation. Adipose tissue-derived mesenchymal stem/stromal cells (AT-MSCs) have shown potential for restoring salivary gland function. However, the mode of action is unknown. The purpose of the present study was therefore to characterize the effect of AT-MSC therapy on the salivary proteome in previously irradiated head and neck cancer patients. METHODS: Whole saliva was collected from patients with radiation-induced salivary gland hypofunction (n = 8) at baseline, and 120 days after AT-MSC treatment, and from healthy controls (n = 10). The salivary proteome was characterized with mass spectrometry based proteomics, and data was compared within the AT-MSC group (baseline versus day 120) and between AT-MSC group and healthy controls. Significance levels between groups were determined by using double-sided t-test, and visualized by means of principal component analysis, volcano plots and cluster analysis. RESULTS: Here we show that 140 human proteins are significantly differentially expressed in saliva from patients with radiation-induced hypofunction versus healthy controls. AT-MSC treatment induce a significant impact on the salivary proteome, as 99 proteins are differentially expressed at baseline vs. 120 days after treatment. However, AT-MSC treatment does not restore healthy conditions, as 212 proteins are significantly differentially expressed in saliva 120 days after AT-MSCs treatment, as compared to healthy controls. CONCLUSION: The results indicate an increase in proteins related to tissue regeneration in AT-MSCs treated patients. Our study demonstrates the impact of AT-MSCs on the salivary proteome, thereby providing insight into the potential mode of action of this novel treatment approach.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Lynggaard, Charlotte Duch","Jersie-Christensen, Rosa","Juhl, Morten","Jensen, Siri Beier","Grønhøj, Christian","Melchiors, Jacob","Jacobsen, Søren","Møller-Hansen, Michael","Herly, Mikkel","Ekblond, Annette","Kastrup, Jens","Fischer-Nielsen, Anne","Belstrøm, Daniel","von Buchwald, Christian"],"cuid":["S03-099.13-716156"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Lynggaard, Charlotte Duch"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intraglandular mesenchymal stem cell treatment induces changes in the salivary proteome of irradiated patients","src":["au","ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s43856-022-00223-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.13-716156","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9735277","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85152465981","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36496530","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-eeefb48a-5a57-4f1f-aed3-cc31af4cf376","ku-febddc54-1f35-4ea3-9db4-78522818b9c6","ruc-f60d526a-95a0-4bd7-9907-a0a1d51b2259"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-91A62BDC54D980B9F098B144227A3062"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s43856-022-00223-3","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/99688848/s43856-022-00223-3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/345513948/s43856_022_00223_3.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Institutledelsen, Odontologi og Oral Sundhed"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte Duch","key":"lynggaardpau","last":"Lynggaard","locid":"48939833-8bab-4e03-82f4-c96cc9441aff","name":"Lynggaard, Charlotte Duch","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","country":"dk","first":"Rosa","key":"jersiechristensenpau","last":"Jersie-Christensen","locid":"079ce232-2a69-46fb-b7af-81eb3607b4d8","name":"Jersie-Christensen, Rosa","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Morten","key":"juhlpau","last":"Juhl","name":"Juhl, Morten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Siri Beier","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"3a38bf2e-6373-4936-9128-a6cbe2ac6a08","name":"Jensen, Siri Beier","orcid":"0000-0003-3698-6337","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Christian","key":"grønhøjpau","last":"Grønhøj","locid":"28f17c21-9acb-47f4-852f-ac4073a2dc20","name":"Grønhøj, Christian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Jacob","key":"melchiorspau","last":"Melchiors","locid":"4cb11730-8e11-4a5e-a910-a9f3435e2d94","name":"Melchiors, Jacob","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"2e4e0e73-2c03-4ba5-9956-e84d75506240","name":"Jacobsen, Søren","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Michael","key":"møllerhansenpau","last":"Møller-Hansen","locid":"191147e6-095b-48a6-9240-af4111b4a7a6","name":"Møller-Hansen, Michael","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Mikkel","key":"herlypau","last":"Herly","name":"Herly, Mikkel","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Annette","key":"ekblondpau","last":"Ekblond","name":"Ekblond, Annette","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Jens","key":"kastruppau","last":"Kastrup","locid":"12c1241f-23da-492c-84b0-36691cb95255","name":"Kastrup, Jens","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Anne","key":"fischernielsenpau","last":"Fischer-Nielsen","name":"Fischer-Nielsen, Anne","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Daniel","key":"belstrømpau","last":"Belstrøm","locid":"9df60a8a-0bbd-4e2e-90fc-0cf48cbe5a00","name":"Belstrøm, Daniel","orcid":"0000-0001-7116-5388","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"vonbuchwaldpau","last":"von Buchwald","locid":"fc76b0d1-1263-48f7-a4d0-685e60bbc1b6","name":"von Buchwald, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6753-8129","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36496530"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s43856-022-00223-3","issn":["2730664X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Communications Medicine","paperid":"160","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Communications Medicine","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85152465981"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-eeefb48a-5a57-4f1f-aed3-cc31af4cf376","ku-febddc54-1f35-4ea3-9db4-78522818b9c6","ruc-f60d526a-95a0-4bd7-9907-a0a1d51b2259"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Intraglandular mesenchymal stem cell treatment induces changes in the salivary proteome of irradiated patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.13-716156","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"No effective therapy exists for the most common long-term side effect of radiation therapy for head and neck cancer (HNC) - xerostomia. The objective was to evaluate safety and provide proof of concept for efficacy of allogeneic adipose tissue-derived mesenchymal stem/stromal cells (AT-MSCs) injected into the major salivary glands of irradiated patients. This open-label, first-in-human, phase 1b, and single-center trial was conducted with repeated measurements days 0, 1, 5, and 30 and 4 months. Eligible patients with objective and subjective signs of radiation-induced salivary gland damage after treatment of oropharyngeal squamous cell carcinoma stages I-II (UICC 8) were enrolled. Twenty-five million cryopreserved AT-MSCs were injected into each submandibular and 50 million AT-MSCs into each parotid gland. Data were collected on adverse events, unstimulated and stimulated whole saliva (UWS and SWS) flow rates and saliva composition, patient-reported outcomes (EORTC QLQ-H&N35 and Xerostomia Questionnaire [XQ]), blood samples and salivary gland scintigraphy. Data were analyzed using repeated measures linear mixed models. Ten patients (7 men, 3 women, 59.5 years [range: 45-70]) were treated in 4 glands. No treatment-related serious adverse events occurred. During 4 months, UWS flow rate increased from 0.13 mL/minute at baseline to 0.18 mL/minute with a change of 0.06 (P =. 0009) mL/minute. SWS flow rate increased from 0.66 mL/minute at baseline to 0.75 mL/minute with a change of 0.09 (P =. 017) mL/minute. XQ summary score decreased by 22.6 units (P =. 0004), EORTC QLQ-H&N35 dry mouth domains decreased by 26.7 (P =. 0013), sticky saliva 23.3 (P =. 0015), and swallowing 10.0 (P =. 0016). Our trial suggests treatment of the major salivary glands with allogenic AT-MSCs is safe, warranting confirmation in larger trials.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Lynggaard, Charlotte Duch","Grønhøj, Christian","Christensen, Robin","Fischer-Nielsen, Anne","Melchiors, Jacob","Specht, Lena","Andersen, Elo","Mortensen, Jann","Oturai, Peter Sandor","Barfod, Gry Hoffmann","Haastrup, Eva Kannik","Møller-Hansen, Michael","Haack-Sørensen, Mandana","Ekblond, Annette","Kastrup, Jens","Jensen, Siri Beier","von Buchwald, Christian"],"cuid":["S03-099.90-026696"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Lynggaard, Charlotte Duch"],"keyword":["Cancer","Clinical trials","Female","Head","Head and Neck Neoplasms radiotherapy","Hematopoietic Stem Cell Transplantation","Humans","IMPACT","LIFE","Male","Mechanisms","Mesenchymal stem cells","Radiation Injuries etiology","SALIVARY","Stem cells","Xerostomia","Xerostomia etiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intraglandular off the shelf allogeneic mesenchymal stem cell treatment in patients with radiation induced xerostomia a safety study mesrix ii","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/stcltm/szac011","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.90-026696","identifier":[{"id":"85131225099","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000786589700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC9154319","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35435231","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c1154a10-f8b7-4d8a-9cec-0d3f8afc6672","ku-ec2d1c7e-c9c4-4ea1-a24c-215e77d2c1cc","sdu-266b0607-11a6-44be-b252-a2915da79334"],"keyword":["Female","HEAD","Head and Neck Neoplasms/radiotherapy","Hematopoietic Stem Cell Transplantation","Humans","IMPACT","LIFE","MECHANISMS","Male","Radiation Injuries/etiology","SALIVARY","Xerostomia/etiology","cancer","clinical trials","mesenchymal stem cells","stem cells","xerostomia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-AB1169BD27614A0D681948A7735F619A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/269065997/szac011.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/203488997/szac011.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/stcltm/szac011","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/320013884/szac011.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg","Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Charlotte Duch","key":"lynggaardpau","last":"Lynggaard","locid":"48939833-8bab-4e03-82f4-c96cc9441aff","name":"Lynggaard, Charlotte Duch","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Christian","key":"grønhøjpau","last":"Grønhøj","locid":"28f17c21-9acb-47f4-852f-ac4073a2dc20","name":"Grønhøj, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"04bf2bf9-a6d8-4be8-93fd-82f3f2ddc9ba","name":"Christensen, Robin","orcid":"0000-0002-6600-0631","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne","key":"fischernielsenpau","last":"Fischer-Nielsen","name":"Fischer-Nielsen, Anne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jacob","key":"melchiorspau","last":"Melchiors","locid":"4cb11730-8e11-4a5e-a910-a9f3435e2d94","name":"Melchiors, Jacob","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lena","key":"spechtpau","last":"Specht","locid":"30cb94c3-320a-4750-a367-f34b2d98696a","name":"Specht, Lena","orcid":"0000-0002-6902-2190","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Elo","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Elo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jann","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"6ab8049c-d821-464b-ad25-c541f1511a41","name":"Mortensen, Jann","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter","key":"oturaipau","last":"Oturai","name":"Oturai, Peter","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gry Hoffmann","key":"barfodpau","last":"Barfod","locid":"16b38cd1-97be-47fc-bde3-5409fc8e3b72","name":"Barfod, Gry Hoffmann","orcid":"0000-0002-7000-0757","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Eva Kannik","key":"haastruppau","last":"Haastrup","name":"Haastrup, Eva Kannik","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael","key":"møllerhansenpau","last":"Møller-Hansen","name":"Møller-Hansen, Michael","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mandana","key":"haacksørensenpau","last":"Haack-Sørensen","name":"Haack-Sørensen, Mandana","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Annette","key":"ekblondpau","last":"Ekblond","name":"Ekblond, Annette","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jens","key":"kastruppau","last":"Kastrup","locid":"12c1241f-23da-492c-84b0-36691cb95255","name":"Kastrup, Jens","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Siri Beier","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"3a38bf2e-6373-4936-9128-a6cbe2ac6a08","name":"Jensen, Siri Beier","orcid":"0000-0003-3698-6337","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"vonbuchwaldpau","last":"von Buchwald","locid":"fc76b0d1-1263-48f7-a4d0-685e60bbc1b6","name":"von Buchwald, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6753-8129","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35435231"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/stcltm/szac011","issn":["21576564","21576580"],"issn_org":["21576564"],"issue":"5","journal":"Stem Cells Translational Medicine","pages":"478-489","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Stem Cells Translational Medicine","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131225099"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c1154a10-f8b7-4d8a-9cec-0d3f8afc6672","ku-ec2d1c7e-c9c4-4ea1-a24c-215e77d2c1cc","sdu-266b0607-11a6-44be-b252-a2915da79334"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Intraglandular Off-the-Shelf Allogeneic Mesenchymal Stem Cell Treatment in Patients with Radiation-Induced Xerostomia : A Safety Study (MESRIX-II)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.90-026696","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Intravenous fluids are recommended for the treatment of patients who are in septic shock, but higher fluid volumes have been associated with harm in patients who are in the intensive care unit (ICU). METHODS: In this international, randomized trial, we assigned patients with septic shock in the ICU who had received at least 1 liter of intravenous fluid to receive restricted intravenous fluid or standard intravenous fluid therapy; patients were included if the onset of shock had been within 12 hours before screening. The primary outcome was death from any cause within 90 days after randomization. RESULTS: We enrolled 1554 patients; 770 were assigned to the restrictive-fluid group and 784 to the standard-fluid group. Primary outcome data were available for 1545 patients (99.4%). In the ICU, the restrictive-fluid group received a median of 1798 ml of intravenous fluid (interquartile range, 500 to 4366); the standard-fluid group received a median of 3811 ml (interquartile range, 1861 to 6762). At 90 days, death had occurred in 323 of 764 patients (42.3%) in the restrictive-fluid group, as compared with 329 of 781 patients (42.1%) in the standard-fluid group (adjusted absolute difference, 0.1 percentage points; 95% confidence interval [CI], -4.7 to 4.9; P = 0.96). In the ICU, serious adverse events occurred at least once in 221 of 751 patients (29.4%) in the restrictive-fluid group and in 238 of 772 patients (30.8%) in the standard-fluid group (adjusted absolute difference, -1.7 percentage points; 99% CI, -7.7 to 4.3). At 90 days after randomization, the numbers of days alive without life support and days alive and out of the hospital were similar in the two groups. CONCLUSIONS: Among adult patients with septic shock in the ICU, intravenous fluid restriction did not result in fewer deaths at 90 days than standard intravenous fluid therapy. (Funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation and others; CLASSIC ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT03668236.).","author_count":91,"contributors":["Meyhoff, Tine S.","Hjortrup, Peter B.","Wetterslev, Jørn","Sivapalan, Praleene","Laake, Jon H.","Cronhjort, Maria","Jakob, Stephan M.","Cecconi, Maurizio","Nalos, Marek","Ostermann, Marlies","Malbrain, Manu","Pettilä, Ville","Møller, Morten H.","Kjær, Maj-Brit N.","Lange, Theis","Overgaard-Steensen, Christian","Brand, Björn A.","Winther-Olesen, Marie","White, Jonathan O.","Quist, Lars","Westergaard, Bo","Jonsson, Andreas B.","Hjortsø, Carl J.S.","Meier, Nick","Jensen, Thomas S.","Engstrøm, Janus","Nebrich, Lars","Andersen-Ranberg, Nina C.","Jensen, Jacob V.","Joseph, Neeliya A.","Poulsen, Lone M.","Herløv, Louise S.","Sølling, Christoffer G.","Pedersen, Susan K.","Knudsen, Kurt K.","Straarup, Therese S.","Vang, Marianne L.","Bundgaard, Helle","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Aagaard, Søren Rosborg","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Russell, Lene","Bestle, Morten H.","Schønemann-Lund, Martin","Brøchner, Anne C.","Elvander, Claes F.","Hoffmann, Søren K.L.","Rasmussen, Michael L.","Martin, Yvonne K.","Friberg, Fredrik F.","Seter, Herman","Aslam, Tayyba N.","Ådnøy, Sigrid","Seidel, Philipp","Strand, Kristian","Johnstad, Bror","Joelsson-Alm, Eva","Christensen, Jens","Ahlstedt, Christian","Pfortmueller, Carmen A.","Siegemund, Martin","Greco, Massimiliano","Raděj, Jaroslav","Kříž, Miroslav","Gould, Doug W.","Rowan, Kathy M.","Mouncey, Paul R.","Perner, Anders","Siegumfeldt, Rine Moulvad","Vestergaard, Stine Rom"],"cuid":["S04-096.18-007689"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["CLASSIC Trial Group"],"corresponding_author":["Perner, Anders"],"country":["Belgium","Czechia","Finland","Italy","Norway","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Charles University","Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust","Guy's and St. Thomas' Hospital","Helsinki University Hospital","Hospit