{"abstract":"Background: Prognosis models based on stepwise regression methods show modest performance in patients with cardiogenic shock (CS). Automated variable selection allows data-driven risk evaluation by recognizing distinct patterns in data. We sought to evaluate an automated variable selection method (least absolute shrinkage and selection operator, LASSO) for predicting 30-day mortality in patients with acute myocardial infarction and CS (AMICS) receiving acute percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) compared to two established scores. Methods and results: Consecutive patients with AMICS receiving acute PCI at one of two tertiary heart centres in Denmark 2010-2017. Patients were divided according to treatment with mechanical circulatory support (MCS); PCI-MCS cohort (n = 220) versus PCI cohort (n = 1180). The latter was divided into a development (2010-2014) and a temporal validation cohort (2015-2017). Cohort-specific LASSO models were based on data obtained before PCI. LASSO models outperformed IABP-SHOCK II and CardShock risk scores in discriminative ability for 30-day mortality in the PCI validation [receiver operating characteristics area under the curve (ROC AUC) 0.80 (95% CI 0.76-0.84) vs 0.73 (95% CI 0.69-0.77) and 0.70 (95% CI 0.65-0.75), respectively, P < 0.01 for both] and PCI-MCS development cohort [ROC AUC 0.77 (95% CI 0.70-0.83) vs 0.64 (95% CI 0.57-0.71) and 0.64 (95% CI 0.57-0.71), respectively, P < 0.01 for both]. Variable influence differed depending on MCS, with age being the most influential factor in the LASSO-PCI model, whereas haematocrit and estimated glomerular filtration rate were the highest-ranking factors in the LASSO-PCI-MCS model. Conclusion: Data-driven prognosis models outperformed established risk scores in patients with AMICS receiving acute PCI and exhibited good discriminative abilities. Observations indicate a potential use of machinelearning to facilitate individualized patient care and targeted interventions in the future.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Povlsen, Amalie L.","Josiassen, Jakob","Möller, Sören","Hassager, Christian","Jensen, Lisette O.","Holmvang, Lene","Schmidt, Henrik","Moller, Jacob E.","Ravn, Hanne B."],"cuid":["S03-096.55-016735"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche"],"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction and cardiogenic shock","Acute percutaneous coronary intervention","Diagnosis","Heart Assist Devices","Humans","Intra Aortic Balloon Pumping","Machine learning","Mechanical circulatory support","Mortality","Myocardial Infarction","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention","Point of Care Systems","Prediction model","Prognosis","Risk Factors","Shock Cardiogenic etiology","Support","Treatment Outcome","Universal definition"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data driven point of care risk model in patients with acute myocardial infarction and cardiogenic shock","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85124871372","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-096.55-016735","identifier":[{"id":"85124871372","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34151353","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000703964000013","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-37f6b6da-d32c-46c6-900f-32f4faf177fd","ku-d13ebf42-f899-4b1e-8edc-7d3e3a1a270c","sdu-6ad36265-1d12-478f-a389-524c250ee1a8"],"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction and cardiogenic shock","Acute percutaneous coronary intervention","DIAGNOSIS","Heart-Assist Devices","Humans","Intra-Aortic Balloon Pumping","MORTALITY","Machine learning","Mechanical circulatory support","Myocardial Infarction","PREDICTION MODEL","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention","Point-of-Care Systems","Prognosis","Risk Factors","SUPPORT","Shock, Cardiogenic/etiology","Treatment Outcome","UNIVERSAL DEFINITION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-78E38C1CFFD09677F4F692A53DCB0484"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Victor Albeck-bygningen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark (SDU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sci