-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e8126b5b-ec90-4a4f-b793-7ebcef7575b6"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Compatibility of Novel Cardiogenic Shock Phenotypes from the Cardiogenic Shock Working Group (CSWG) with the SCAI Staging System","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-639649","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Importance: Sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitors (SGLT2i) improve outcomes in patients with heart failure and a reduced ejection fraction (HFrEF). The association with cardiac remodeling has not been investigated. Objective: To investigate the outcome of the SGLT2i empagliflozin, compared with placebo, on cardiac remodeling in patients with HFrEF. Design, Setting, and Participants: This exploratory post hoc analysis included participants with stable HFrEF and ejection fractions of 40% or less, who were randomly enrolled in an investigator-initiated, multicenter, double-blind, placebo-controlled randomized clinical trial in Denmark. Enrollment commenced on June 29, 2017, and continued through September 10, 2019, with the last participant follow-up on December 20, 2019. Interventions: Randomization (1:1) to empagliflozin (10 mg once daily) or matching placebo in addition to recommended heart failure therapy for 12 weeks. Main Outcomes and Measures: Efficacy measures were changes from baseline to week 12 in left ventricular end-systolic and end-diastolic volume indexes, left atrial volume index, and left ventricular ejection fraction adjusted for age, sex, type 2 diabetes, and atrial fibrillation. Secondary efficacy measures included changes in left ventricular mass index, global longitudinal strain, and relative wall thickness. Results: A total of 190 patients were randomized (95 each receiving empagliflozin and placebo), with a mean (SD) age of 64 (11) years; 162 were men (85.3%), 97 (51.1%) had ischemic HFrEF, 24 (12.6%) had type 2 diabetes, and the mean (SD) latest recorded left ventricular ejection fraction was 29% (8%). Of the 190, 186 completed the study. Empagliflozin significantly reduced left ventricular end-systolic volume index (-4.3 [95% CI, -8.5 to -0.1] mL/m2; P =.04), left ventricular end-diastolic volume index (-5.5 [95% CI, -10.6 to -0.4] mL/m2; P =.03), and left atrial volume index (-2.5 [95% CI, -4.8 to -0.1] mL/m2; P =.04) compared with placebo at 12 weeks' follow-up, with no change in left ventricular ejection fraction (1.2% [95% CI, -1.2% to 3.6%]; P =.32). These findings were consistent across subgroups. Of secondary efficacy measures, left ventricular mass index was significantly reduced by empagliflozin (-9.0 [95% CI, -17.2 to -0.8] g/m2; P =.03). Conclusions and Relevance: In this small, randomized, short-term study, empagliflozin was associated with modest reductions in left ventricular and left atrial volumes with no association with ejection fraction. Effects beyond 12 weeks of SGLT2i use require further study. Trial Registration: ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT03198585.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Omar, Massar","Jensen, Jesper","Ali, Mulham","Frederiksen, Peter H.","Kistorp, Caroline","Videbæk, Lars","Poulsen, Mikael Kjær","Tuxen, Christian D.","Möller, Sören","Gustafsson, Finn","Køber, Lars","Schou, Morten","Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-039710"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Omar, Massar"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"associations of empagliflozin with left ventricular volumes mass and function in patients with heart failure and reduced ejection fraction a substudy of the empire hf randomized clinical trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7788505","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-039710","identifier":[{"id":"33404637","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7788505","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85099206047","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-012aa49e-d014-4fe3-b97e-212d7276976e","sdu-bf277c0a-fbb4-41b1-8eda-4a7eeac57b07"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E6214EAC94CB1610AA9A3AAFD618149A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7788505","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of SDCO - Steno Diabetes Center Odense"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Massar","key":"omarpau","last":"Omar","locid":"3a6641e9-a451-482c-a139-b60841705f94","name":"Omar, Massar","orcid":"0000-0002-9634-3889","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e9d2d407-3550-4e0e-a0da-a9770d60e5a0","name":"Jensen, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mulham","key":"alipau","last":"Ali","locid":"c5edf0d7-b5bb-496e-87f9-67dee7af19a9","name":"Ali, Mulham","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter H.","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"85d6facd-93bf-44ee-a117-269fb26a52be","name":"Frederiksen, Peter H.","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-7980","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Caroline","key":"kistorppau","last":"Kistorp","locid":"42328645-d772-4f53-9f70-438ff40291b9","name":"Kistorp, Caroline","orcid":"0000-0002-3019-6775","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"videbækpau","last":"Videbæk","locid":"c0abdf18-4e26-411a-99c3-de3cbe029dee","name":"Videbæk, Lars","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikael Kjær","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"a8da3614-e99d-403f-933f-f5dfab3976af","name":"Poulsen, Mikael Kjær","orcid":"0000-0003-4051-7197","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian D.","key":"tuxenpau","last":"Tuxen","name":"Tuxen, Christian D.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sören","key":"möllerpau","last":"Möller","locid":"905018dc-c6c4-4a79-b50d-d0c08618e77a","name":"Möller, Sören","orcid":"0000-0003-0858-4269","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Finn","key":"gustafssonpau","last":"Gustafsson","locid":"6716eef1-891b-4209-a823-e96e765b9433","name":"Gustafsson, Finn","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Morten","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"48fa6ec9-1941-4566-b931-14b0cc8cbae3","name":"Schou, Morten","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33404637"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamacardio.2020.6827","issn":["23806583","23806591"],"issn_org":["23806583"],"issue":"7","journal":"JAMA Cardiology","pages":"836-840","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA Cardiology","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85099206047"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-012aa49e-d014-4fe3-b97e-212d7276976e","sdu-bf277c0a-fbb4-41b1-8eda-4a7eeac57b07"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Associations of Empagliflozin with Left Ventricular Volumes, Mass, and Function in Patients with Heart Failure and Reduced Ejection Fraction : A Substudy of the Empire HF Randomized Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-039710","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Cardiogenic shock (CS) is a heterogeneous syndrome with varied presentations and outcomes. We used a machine learning approach to test the hypothesis that patients with CS have distinct phenotypes at presentation, which are associated with unique clinical profiles and in-hospital mortality. METHODS AND RESULTS: We analyzed data from 1959 patients with CS from 2 international cohorts: CSWG (Cardiogenic Shock Working Group Registry) (myocardial infarction [CSWG-MI; n=410] and acute-on-chronic heart failure [CSWG-HF; n=480]) and the DRR (Danish Retroshock MI Registry) (n=1069). Clusters of patients with CS were identified in CSWG-MI using the consensus k means algorithm and subsequently validated in CSWG-HF and DRR. Patients in each phenotype were further categorized by their Society of Cardiovascular Angiography and Interventions staging. The machine learning algorithms revealed 3 distinct clusters in CS: \"non-congested (I)\", \"cardiorenal (II),\" and \"cardiometabolic (III)\" shock. Among the 3 cohorts (CSWG-MI versus DDR versus CSWG-HF), in-hospital mortality was 21% versus 28% versus 10%, 45% versus 40% versus 32%, and 55% versus 56% versus 52% for clusters I, II, and III, respectively. The \"cardiometabolic shock\" cluster had the highest risk of developing stage D or E shock as well as in-hospital mortality among the phenotypes, regardless of cause. Despite baseline differences, each cluster showed reproducible demographic, metabolic, and hemodynamic profiles across the 3 cohorts. CONCLUSIONS: Using machine learning, we identified and validated 3 distinct CS phenotypes, with specific and reproducible associations with mortality. These phenotypes may allow for targeted patient enrollment in clinical trials and foster development of tailored treatment strategies in subsets of patients with CS.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Zweck, Elric","Thayer, Katherine L.","Helgestad, Ole K.L.","Kanwar, Manreet","Ayouty, Mohyee","Garan, A. Reshad","Hernandez-Montfort, Jaime","Mahr, Claudius","Wencker, Detlef","Sinha, Shashank S.","Vorovich, Esther","Abraham, Jacob","O’neill, William","Li, Song","Hickey, Gavin W.","Josiassen, Jakob","Hassager, Christian","Jensen, Lisette O.","Holmvang, Lene","Schmidt, Henrik","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Møller, Jacob E.","Burkhoff, Daniel","Kapur, Navin K."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-040288"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kapur, Navin K."],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Allegheny Health Network","Baylor Scott & White Advanced Heart Failure Clinic","Baylor Scott & White Health","Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center","Cardiovascular Research Foundation","Cleveland Clinic","Cleveland Clinic Florida","Harvard University","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Henry Ford Health System","Henry Ford Hospital","Inova Heart and Vascular Institute","Northwestern Medicine","Providence Heart Institute","Tufts Medical Center","Tufts University","University of Pittsburgh","University of Pittsburgh Medical Center","University of Washington","University of Washington Medical Center","Western Pennsylvania Hospital"],"keyword":["Cardiogenic shock","Clusters","Heart failure","Hemodynamics","Machine learning","Myocardial Infarction","Phenotypes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phenotyping cardiogenic shock","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.120.020085","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Dr Garan is an unpaid consultant for Abiomed Inc. Dr Hernandez-Montfort is a consultant for Abiomed Inc (research and education). Dr Burkhoff reports an unrestricted, educational grant from Abiomed Inc to Cardiovascular Research Foundation. Dr Vorovich is a consultant and in the speakers’ bureau of Abiomed Inc. Dr Abraham is a consultant for Abbott Laboratories and Abiomed Inc. Dr Møller receives speaker honoraria and a research grant from Abiomed Inc. Dr Kapur receives consulting/speaker honoraria and institutional grant support from: Abbott Laboratories, Abiomed Inc, Boston Scientific, Edwards, Medtronic, Getinge, LivaNova, MDStart, Precardia, and Zoll. Dr Sinha is a consultant for Abiomed Inc (Critical Care Advisory Board). Dr O’Neill receives consulting/speaker honoraria from Abiomed Inc, Boston Scientific Inc, and Abbott Laboratories. None of the listed disclosures could be perceived as a competing interest for the content of this article. The remaining authors have no disclosures to report. This work was supported by a NIH RO1 grant to NKK (RO1HL139785-01) and institutional grants from Abbott Laboratories Inc (Abbott Park, IL), Abiomed Inc (Danvers, MA), Boston Scientific Inc (Minneapolis, MN), and Getinge Inc (Wayne, NJ) to Tufts Medical Center and by a grant from the Danish Heart Foundation (16-R107-A6576) to OKLH."],"id":"S02-100.00-040288","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8483502","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34227396","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85111038945","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-11bd6cd4-4da3-4622-90e6-59b0e856f44a","sdu-6f3829c4-d160-457b-854b-23763ea41865"],"keyword":["Cardiogenic shock","Clusters","Heart failure","Hemodynamics","Machine learning","Myocardial infarction","Phenotypes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-246B6D4D357919DAD40101CAACA57A03"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/185030087/JAHA.120.020085.pdf","version