s":"1807-1817","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA  The Journal of the American Medical Association","title_org":"JAMA: The Journal of the American Medical Association","volume":"326"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117849363"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-04a329c2-9c2e-411e-8d5b-9bf36f405df6","ku-3be6af16-cc79-4e8d-99d8-4059f7427692"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of 12 mg vs 6 mg of Dexamethasone on the Number of Days Alive Without Life Support in Adults With COVID-19 and Severe Hypoxemia : The COVID STEROID 2 Randomized Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.88-792759","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT: In patients with ST-elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI) the immune system is activated with an inflammatory response to follow. In STEMI patients with a severe inflammatory response, risk of development of cardiogenic shock (CS) seems increased. Neutrophil Gelatinase-Associated Lipocalin (NGAL) is a glycoprotein released from mature neutrophils and plasma concentration may increase immediately after STEMI. We therefore aimed to assess whether admission NGAL plasma concentration in patients with STEMI was associated with CS development after leaving the catheterization laboratory (late CS) and 30-day all-cause mortality. PATIENTS AND METHODS: From 1,892 consecutive patients with STEMI 1,626 (86%) had plasma NGAL concentration measured upon hospital admission before angiography throughout a 1-year period at two tertiary heart centers in Denmark. Patients were stratified according to NGAL quartiles (Q1-4). To assess late CS development, we adjusted for the Observatoire Régional Breton sur l'Infarctus risk score for late CS. For mortality assessment, we adjusted for gender, age, post-PCI culprit Thrombolysis in myocardial infarction flow, left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF), kidney dysfunction, and being comatose after cardiac arrest. RESULTS: Increasing NGAL concentration was associated with higher age, more comorbidities, and more critical patient conditions including lower blood pressure and LVEF. When adjusted for factors associated with poor outcome, NGAL remained independently associated with both late CS development (Q4 vs. Q1-3) (OR (95% CI) 3.64 (1.79-7.41) and 30-day mortality (HR (95% CI) 3.18 (1.73-5.84)). CONCLUSION: Admission plasma concentration of NGAL in STEMI patients is independently associated with 30-day all-cause mortality and predictive of late CS development.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Frydland, Martin","Møgelvang, Rasmus","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Helgestad, Ole K. L.","Holmvang, Lene","Mark, Peter D.","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-091.49-046520"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Frydland, Martin"],"keyword":["Cardiogenic shock","Inflammation","Neutrophil gelatinase associated lipocalin","ST elevation myocardial infarction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neutrophil gelatinase associated lipocalin ngal measured at admission is associated with development of late cardiogenic shock and mortality in patients with st segment elevation myocardial infarction","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85111805236","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-091.49-046520","identifier":[{"id":"34276039","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85111805236","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d57f7196-8270-4156-8abd-c712458ec742","sdu-07525d3d-6f2c-4bf8-b3f0-555fb728fb66"],"keyword":["Cardiogenic shock","ST-elevation myocardial infarction","inflammation","neutrophil gelatinase-associated lipocalin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6C4021446EEC378C63C97D30441E85C4"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Medicine (Svendborg)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"frydlandpau","last":"Frydland","name":"Frydland, Martin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1 3","first":"Rasmus","key":"møgelvangpau","last":"Møgelvang","locid":"0863bdef-1d17-423f-b966-d42aba8df925","name":"Møgelvang, Rasmus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole K.L.","key":"helgestadpau","last":"Helgestad","locid":"ab9f3165-500c-482b-9c2f-1879b3abedb3","name":"Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","name_org":"Helgestad, Ole K.L.","orcid":"0000-0003-3847-8758","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Lene","key":"holmvangpau","last":"Holmvang","locid":"54b8ef01-f8ed-4c49-a126-2109e2fd351f","name":"Holmvang, Lene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter D.","key":"markpau","last":"Mark","name":"Mark, Peter D.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette Okkels","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34276039"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/shk.0000000000001721","issn":["10732322","15400514"],"issn_org":["10732322"],"issue":"2","journal":"Shock","pages":"255-259","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Shock","title_org":"Shock (Augusta, Ga.)","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111805236"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d57f7196-8270-4156-8abd-c712458ec742","sdu-07525d3d-6f2c-4bf8-b3f0-555fb728fb66"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Neutrophil Gelatinase-Associated Lipocalin (NGAL) Measured at Admission is Associated With Development of Late Cardiogenic Shock and Mortality in Patients With ST-Segment Elevation Myocardial Infarction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.49-046520","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Pathogenic variants in the X-linked gene NEXMIF (previously KIAA2022) are associated with intellectual disability (ID), autism spectrum disorder, and epilepsy. We aimed to delineate the female and male phenotypic spectrum of NEXMIF encephalopathy. Methods: Through an international collaboration, we analyzed the phenotypes and genotypes of 87 patients with NEXMIF encephalopathy. Results: Sixty-three females and 24 males (46 new patients) with NEXMIF encephalopathy were studied, with 30 novel variants. Phenotypic features included developmental delay/ID in 86/87 (99%), seizures in 71/86 (83%) and multiple comorbidities. Generalized seizures predominated including myoclonic seizures and absence seizures (both 46/70, 66%), absence with eyelid myoclonia (17/70, 24%), and atonic seizures (30/70, 43%). Males had more severe developmental impairment; females had epilepsy more frequently, and varied from unaffected to severely affected. All NEXMIF pathogenic variants led to a premature stop codon or were deleterious structural variants. Most arose de novo, although X-linked segregation occurred for both sexes. Somatic mosaicism occurred in two males and a family with suspected parental mosaicism. Conclusion: NEXMIF encephalopathy is an X-linked, generalized developmental and epileptic encephalopathy characterized by myoclonic–atonic epilepsy overlapping with eyelid myoclonia with absence. Some patients have developmental encephalopathy without epilepsy. Males have more severe developmental impairment. NEXMIF encephalopathy arises due to loss-of-function variants.","author_count":86,"contributors":["Stamberger, Hannah","Hammer, Trine B.","Gardella, Elena","Vlaskamp, Danique R.M.","Bertelsen, Birgitte","Mandelstam, Simone","de Lange, Iris","Zhang, Jing","Myers, Candace T.","Fenger, Christina","Afawi, Zaid","Almanza Fuerte, Edith P.","Andrade, Danielle M.","Balcik, Yunus","Ben Zeev, Bruria","Bennett, Mark F.","Berkovic, Samuel F.","Isidor, Bertrand","Bouman, Arjan","Brilstra, Eva","Busk, Øyvind L.","Cairns, Anita","Caumes, Roseline","Chatron, Nicolas","Dale, Russell C.","de Geus, Christa","Edery, Patrick","Gill, Deepak","Granild-Jensen, Jacob Bie","Gunderson, Lauren","Gunning, Boudewijn","Heimer, Gali","Helle, Johan R.","Hildebrand, Michael S.","Hollingsworth, Georgie","Kharytonov, Volodymyr","Klee, Eric W.","Koeleman, Bobby P.C.","Koolen, David A.","Korff, Christian","Küry, Sébastien","Lesca, Gaetan","Lev, Dorit","Leventer, Richard J.","Mackay, Mark T.","Macke, Erica L.","McEntagart, Meriel","Mohammad, Shekeeb S.","Monin, Pauline","Montomoli, Martino","Morava, Eva","Moutton, Sebastien","Muir, Alison M.","Parrini, Elena","Procopis, Peter","Ranza, Emmanuelle","Reed, Laura","Reif, Philipp S.","Rosenow, Felix","Rossi, Massimiliano","Sadleir, Lynette G.","Sadoway, Tara","Schelhaas, Helenius J.","Schneider, Amy L.","Shah, Krati","Shalev, Ruth","Sisodiya, Sanjay M.","Smol, Thomas","Stumpel, Connie T.R.M.","Stuurman, Kyra","Symonds, Joseph D.","Mau-Them, Frederic Tran","Verbeek, Nienke","Verhoeven, Judith S.","Wallace, Geoffrey","Yosovich, Keren","Zarate, Yuri A.","Zerem, Ayelet","Zuberi, Sameer M.","Guerrini, Renzo","Mefford, Heather C.","Patel, Chirag","Zhang, Yue Hua","Møller, Rikke S.","Scheffer, Ingrid E."],"cuid":["S02-093.18-028991"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Scheffer, Ingrid E."],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Canada","China","France","Germany","India","Israel","Italy","Lebanon","Netherlands","New Zealand","Norway","Switzerland","Ukraine","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Antwerp University Hospital","Auditory Cognition and Psychoacoustics Team","CPDPN","Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","Central Mancheste