{"abstract":"We demonstrate the efficiency of a recent exact-gradient optimal control methodology by applying it to a challenging many-body problem, crossing the superfluid to Mott-insulator phase transition in the Bose-Hubbard model. The system size necessitates a matrix product state representation and this seamlessly integrates with the requirements of the algorithm. We observe fidelities in the range 0.99–0.9999 with associated minimal process duration estimates displaying an exponential fidelity-duration trade-off across several orders of magnitude. The corresponding optimal solutions are characterized in terms of a predominantly linear sweep across the critical point followed by bang-bang-like structure. This is quite different from the smooth and monotonic solutions identified by earlier gradient-free optimizations which are hampered in locating the higher complexity protocols in the regime of high fidelities at low process durations. Overall, the comparison suggests significant methodological improvements also for many-body systems in the ideal open-loop setting. Acknowledging that idealized open-loop control may deteriorate in actual experiments, we discuss the merits of using such an approach in combination with closed-loop control—in particular, high-fidelity physical insights extracted with the former can be used to formulate practical, low-dimensional search spaces for the latter.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jensen, Jesper Hasseriis Mohr","Møller, Frederik Skovbo","Sørensen, Jens Jakob Winther H","Sherson, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-215466"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Jesper Hasseriis Mohr","Sherson, Jacob"],"country":["Austria"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Vienna University of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"achieving fast high fidelity optimal control of many body quantum dynamics","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2008.06076.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-215466","identifier":[{"id":"85119196774","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-973167ec-fc14-48db-9e4d-11da8cce98e9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F4B18A52B7D18EA7F98530FF38600A85"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2008.06076.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Physics and Astronomy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"vienna university of technology","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Vienna University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Hasseriis Mohr","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"90e2a5b6-a5b4-46be-b61b-3e1140888954","name":"Jensen, Jesper Hasseriis Mohr","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik Skovbo","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Frederik Skovbo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Jakob Winther H","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5ce4a9ba-0fd6-404b-bdf7-0e9ae99b5891","name":"Sørensen, Jens Jakob Winther H","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"shersonpau","last":"Sherson","locid":"3d8e1590-c4fa-495b-81b4-588fe374b36c","name":"Sherson, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-6048-587X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physreva.104.052210","issn":["24699926","24699934"],"issn_org":["24699926"],"issue":"5","journal":"Physical Review A","paperid":"052210","publisher":"American Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Physical Review A","volume":"104"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85119196774"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-973167ec-fc14-48db-9e4d-11da8cce98e9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Achieving fast high-fidelity optimal control of many-body quantum dynamics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-215466","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
