{"abstract":"Accurate derivatives are important for efficiently locally traversing and converging in quantum optimization landscapes. By deriving analytically exact control derivatives (gradient and Hessian), we show here that the feasibility of meeting this central accuracy requirement critically depends on the choice of propagation scheme and problem representation. Even when exact propagation is sufficiently cheap it is, perhaps surprisingly, much more efficient to optimize the (appropriately) approximate propagators: in a certain sense, approximations in the dynamics are traded off for significant complexity reductions in the exact derivative calculations. Importantly, past the initial analytical considerations, only standard numerical techniques are explicitly required with straightforward application to realistic systems.These results are numerically verified for two concrete problems of increasing Hilbert space dimensionality. The best schemes obtain unit fidelity to machine precision, whereas the results for other schemes are separated consistently by orders of magnitude in computation time and in worst case 10 orders of magnitude in achievable fidelity. Since these gaps continually increase with system size and complexity, this methodology unlocks efficient optimization of many-body dynamics operating in the unprecedented high-fidelity regime which will be published separately.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jensen, Jesper Hasseriis Mohr","Møller, Frederik Skovbo","Sørensen, Jens Jakob Winther H","Sherson, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-257322"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sherson, Jacob"],"country":["Austria"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Vienna University of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"approximate dynamics lead to more optimal control efficient exact derivatives","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.09943","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-257322","ids":["au-e03b10c7-48f5-4006-80ab-51211ec574a5"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A15A13B9B520A31D99A75D6AFC9CEC68"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.09943","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Physics and Astronomy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"vienna university of technology","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Vienna University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Hasseriis Mohr","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"90e2a5b6-a5b4-46be-b61b-3e1140888954","name":"Jensen, Jesper Hasseriis Mohr","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik Skovbo","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Frederik Skovbo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Jakob Winther H","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5ce4a9ba-0fd6-404b-bdf7-0e9ae99b5891","name":"Sørensen, Jens Jakob Winther H","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"shersonpau","last":"Sherson","locid":"3d8e1590-c4fa-495b-81b4-588fe374b36c","name":"Sherson, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-6048-587X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"arXiv","publisher_org":"ArXiv","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e03b10c7-48f5-4006-80ab-51211ec574a5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Approximate Dynamics Lead to More Optimal Control : Efficient Exact Derivatives","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-257322","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) is a major threat to global health, and it is crucial to understand the epidemiological aspects in order to predict the emergence and propagation of AMR genes. The aim of this study was to assess the variability and medium-term AMR trends within the mostly healthy human population of a single city. We monitored over 36 months (November 2015 to November 2018) the AMR level in the city of Copenhagen, Denmark, by taking bi-weekly sewage samples from the inlets of the three main water treatment plants, extracting the DNA, performing metagenomic sequencing, and read-mapping against a database of known AMR genes. We found that the AMR level was surprisingly stable with no periodic variability and no signs of drift over the measured period. We found, however, that the seemingly random variations at each site correlate in time with each other, suggesting that the variations we see are due to real environmental changes in the occurrence of AMR.IMPORTANCE The Copenhagen sewage resistome is surprisingly stable in time. The implication is that, at least for cities that are comparable to Copenhagen in terms of sewer infrastructure, few or even single samples provide a robust picture of the resistome within a city.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Brinch, Christian","Leekitcharoenphon, Pimlapas","Ribeiro Duarte, Ana Sofia","Svendsen, Christina Aaby","Jensen, Jacob Dyring","Aarestrup, Frank Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-311033"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Brinch, Christian"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term temporal stability of the resistome in sewage from copenhagen","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/mSystems.00841-20","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-311033","identifier":[{"id":"85095450639","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7577296","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33082278","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-15681b12-c4a7-4c84-b36d-db9706232654"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-67E0403B0409A78678C324CB82319289"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/mSystems.00841-20","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/222471675/mSystems_2020_Brinch_e00841_20.full_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Genomic Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"brinchpau","last":"Brinch","locid":"b4feaf3e-89fc-4b47-b132-cfe7fc2903dc","name":"Brinch, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-5074-7183","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pimlapas","key":"leekitcharoenphonpau","last":"Leekitcharoenphon","locid":"432b3315-1807-49ee-a83f-d4ea2a9219d1","name":"Leekitcharoenphon, Pimlapas","orcid":"0000-0002-5674-0142","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ana Sofia Ribeiro","key":"duartepau","last":"Duarte","locid":"f4843775-d9f2-4b55-964f-94521776787a","name":"Ribeiro Duarte, Ana Sofia","name_org":"Duarte, Ana Sofia Ribeiro","orcid":"0000-0002-8794-0542","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christina Aaby","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"92b0691c-cbf6-49f9-b150-5c018753ff88","name":"Svendsen, Christina Aaby","orcid":"0000-0002-2532-6854","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Dyring","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"0c03557e-9e42-4e40-afb3-fd3e6c70260e","name":"Jensen, Jacob Dyring","orcid":"0009-0003-5155-3633","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frank Møller","key":"aarestruppau","last":"Aarestrup","locid":"8a1eb030-2c37-4557-bce1-7bc6d5c75aaa","name":"Aarestrup, Frank Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-7116-2723","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33082278"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/msystems.00841-20","issn":["23795077"],"issue":"5","journal":"mSystems","paperid":"e00841-20","publisher":"American Society for Microbiology","status":"p","title":"mSystems","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85095450639"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-15681b12-c4a7-4c84-b36d-db9706232654"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Long-Term Temporal Stability of the Resistome in Sewage from Copenhagen","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-311033","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Concomitant vasoactive drugs are often required to maintain adequate perfusion pressure in patients with acute myocardial infarction (AMI) and cardiogenic shock (CS) receiving hemodynamic support with an axial flow pump (Impella CP). OBJECTIVE: To compare the effect of equipotent dosages of epinephrine, dopamine, norepinephrine, and phenylephrine on cardiac work and end-organ perfusion in a porcine model of profound ischemic CS supported with an Impella CP. METHODS: CS was induced in 10 pigs by stepwise intracoronary injection of polyvinyl microspheres. Hemodynamic support with Impella CP was initiated followed by blinded crossover to vasoactive treatment with norepinephrine (0.10 μg/kg/min), epinephrine (0.10 μg/kg/min), or dopamine (10 μg/kg/min) for 30 min each. At the end of the study, phenylephrine (10 μg/kg/min) was administered for 20 min. The primary outcome was cardiac workload, a product of pressure-volume area (PVA) and heart rate (HR), measured using the conductance catheter technique. End-organ perfusion was assessed by measuring venous oxygen saturation from the pulmonary artery (SvO2), jugular bulb, and renal vein. Treatment effects were evaluated using multilevel mixed-effects linear regression. RESULTS: All catecholamines significantly increased LV stroke work and cardiac work, dopamine to the greatest extend by 341.8 × 103 (mmHg × mL)/min [95% CI (174.1, 509.5), p < 0.0001], and SvO2 significantly improved during all catecholamines. Phenylephrine, a vasoconstrictor, caused a significant increase in cardiac work by 437.8 × 103 (mmHg × mL)/min [95% CI (297.9, 577.6), p < 0.0001] due to increase in potential energy (p = 0.001), but no significant change in LV stroke work. Also, phenylephrine tended to decrease SvO2 (p = 0.063) and increased arterial lactate levels (p = 0.002). CONCLUSION: Catecholamines increased end-organ perfusion at the expense of increased cardiac work, most by dopamine. However, phenylephrine increased cardiac work with no increase in end-organ perfusion.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Udesen, Nanna L J","Helgestad, Ole K L","Banke, Ann B S","Frederiksen, Peter H","Josiassen, Jakob","Jensen, Lisette O","Schmidt, Henrik","Edelman, Elazer R","Chang, Brian Y","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Møller, Jacob E"],"cuid":["S02-086.79-046211"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard Medical School","Massachusetts Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction","Animals","Cardiac Output drug effects","Cardiac work","Cardiogenic shock","Catecholamines therapeutic use","Disease Models Animal","Dopamine","Heart Assist Devices","Hemodynamics drug effects","Humans","Mechanical circulatory support","Myocardial Infarction complications","Norepinephrine","Organ perfusion","Phenylephrine","Shock Cardiogenic physiopathology","Swine","Vasopressor"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of concomitant vasoactive treatment and mechanical left ventricular unloading in a porcine model of profound cardiogenic shock","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-020-2816-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.79-046211","identifier":[{"id":"32188462","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7079533","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85081997829","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-caea6cd6-546b-4163-9b63-486f0f5a9365","sdu-29d055d0-4138-479b-901b-c96d776ffc29"],"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction","Animals","Cardiac Output/drug effects","Cardiac work","Cardiogenic shock","Catecholamines/therapeutic use","Disease Models, Animal","Dopamine","Heart-Assist Devices","Hemodynamics/drug effects","Humans","Mechanical circulatory support","Myocardial Infarction/complications","Norepinephrine","Organ perfusion","Phenylephrine","Shock, Cardiogenic/physiopathology","Swine","Vasopressor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CE6DF4C67CF66AED1386B71FA932326D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/252295426/s13054_020_2816_8.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13054-020-2816-8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/168787916/s13054_020_2816_8.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Mental Health Services Glostrup"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"massachusetts institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country