","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","name":"Berg, Selina Kikkenborg","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"J.E","key":"mollerpau","last":"Moller","name":"Moller, J.E","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"A. V.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, A. V.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ola","key":"ekholmpau","last":"Ekholm","locid":"b59d640e-8087-46d7-8284-5a45e6ebd03f","name":"Ekholm, Ola","orcid":"0000-0002-5563-7098","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Elmose","key":"molspau","last":"Mols","name":"Mols, Rikke Elmose","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"C.B","key":"thoruppau","last":"Thorup","locid":"90bf6dfd-49cd-42dc-a945-c22f8561c981","name":"Thorup, Charlotte Brun","name_org":"Thorup, C.B","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"T. B.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, T. B.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ehjci/ehaa946.3417","issn":["0195668X","15229645"],"issn_org":["0195668X"],"issue":"Suppl. 2","journal":"European Heart Journal","pages":"3417","paperid":"ehaa946.3417","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-40447f93-940a-42fa-9ca5-3edbd40b5631","sdu-e3841da3-03cb-4477-bc50-400778b737bf"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Symptoms of depression at discharge after PCI are associated with an increased risk of 1-year mortality : findings from the national DenHeart study","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.50-003157","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To compare the effect of equipotent dosages of epinephrine, dopamine, norepinephrine, and phenylephrine on left ventricular (LV) work and end-organ perfusion in a porcine model of profound ischemic cardiogenic shock (CS) supported by Impella CP. METHODS: CS was induced in 10 pigs by stepwise intracoronary injection of microspheres. After CS was induced and Impella CP support initiated, animals were treated in a blinded crossover design with norepinephrine (0.10 µg/kg/min), epinephrine (0.10 µg/kg/min) or dopamine (10 µg/kg/min) for 30 minutes each. Phenylephrine (10 µg/kg/min) was given at the end of the study for 20 minutes. LV work was estimated using a conductance catheter. Main outcome measure was LV work estimated by pressure volume area (PVA) x heart rate. End-organ perfusion was evaluated by mixed venous oxygen saturation (SVO2) from the pulmonary artery and arterial lactate levels. Multilevel mixed-effects linear regression was used to evaluate treatment effect. RESULTS: All vasoactive drugs induced a significant increase in LV work, borderline for norepinephrine by 92.4 (mmHg*mL)*103/min ⦋95%CI(-1.1, 186), p=0.053)⦌. For all catecholamines, stroke work was significantly increased, but unchanged with phenylephrine, which on the other hand caused a significant increase in potential energy by 483 mmHg*mL ⦋95%CI(195, 772), p=0.001)⦌. SVO2 increased significantly with catecholamines and decreased borderline with phenylephrine by -9 %point ⦋95%CI(-19, 0.49), p=0.063)⦌ which also increased arterial lactate levels by 2.4 mmol/L ⦋95%CI(0.89, 3.92), p=0.002)⦌. There was a trend toward lower arterial lactate levels with norepinephrine by -1.53 mmol/L ⦋95%CI(-3.15, 0.09), p=0.064)⦌ CONCLUSION: Catecholamines increased SVO2 but at the expense of increased LV work, least for norepinephrine and highest for dopamine (figure). Isolated vasoconstriction (phenylephrine) caused an increase in LV work, a decrease in SVO2 and increase in arterial lactate levels.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Banke, Ann","Frederiksen, Peter H.","Jossiasen, J.","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Schmidt, Henrik","Ravn, H. B.","Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-638697"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of concomitant vasoactive treatment in mechanical left ventricular unloading in profound cardiogenic shock","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-638697","identifier":[{"id":"32465765","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-e4b55be3-ad0f-45a4-8d7d-50052f21d068"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-81D2C0AE1BA510A5900E94685FC586E7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"N. J.","key":"udesenpau","last":"Udesen","locid":"f71f56f5-4f36-4de5-a7ae-e5e51f101a83","name":"Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","name_org":"Udesen, N. J.","orcid":"0000-0003-1542-3260","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"O. K.","key":"helgestadpau","last":"Helgestad","locid":"ab9f3165-500c-482b-9c2f-1879b3abedb3","name":"Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","name_org":"Helgestad, O. K.","orcid":"0000-0003-3847-8758","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"bankepau","last":"Banke","locid":"0d350637-c6ce-4cf8-82ba-e965da703690","name":"Banke, Ann","name_org":"Banke, A.","orcid":"0000-0002-1036-580X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"P. H.","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"85d6facd-93bf-44ee-a117-269fb26a52be","name":"Frederiksen, Peter H.","name_org":"Frederiksen, P. H.","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-7980","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"jossiasenpau","last":"Jossiasen","name":"Jossiasen, J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L. O.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","name_org":"Jensen, L. O.","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"H.","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","name_org":"Schmidt, H.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"H. B.","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","name":"Ravn, H. B.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J. E.","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","name_org":"Møller, J. E.","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32465765"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.healun.2020.01.268","issn":["10532498","15573117"],"issn_org":["10532498"],"issue":"4 Suppl.","journal":"Journal of Heart and Lung Transplantation","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Heart and Lung Transplantation","title_org":"The Journal of Heart and Lung Transplantation","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e4b55be3-ad0f-45a4-8d7d-50052f21d068"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Impact of Concomitant Vasoactive Treatment in Mechanical Left Ventricular Unloading in Profound Cardiogenic Shock","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-638697","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To validate the IABP-SHOCK II risk score in a Danish cohort and assess the association between the IABP-SHOCK II risk score and admission concentration of biomarkers reflecting neurohormonal - (Copeptin, Pro-atrial natriuretic peptide (proANP), Mid-regional pro-adrenomedullin (MRproADM)) and inflammatory (ST2) activation in patients with CS complicating ST segment elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI). METHODS: A total of 137 consecutive patients admitted with STEMI and CS at two tertiary heart centres were stratified according to the IABP-SHOCK II risk score (0-2; 3/4; 5-9), and had blood sampled upon admission. RESULTS: Plasma concentrations of Copeptin (median (pmol/L) score 0-2: 313; score 3/4: 682; score 5-9: 632 p < 0.0001), proANP (pmol/L) (1459; 2225; 2876 p = 0.0009) and MRproADM (nmol/L) (0.86; 1.2; 1.4 p = 0.04) were significantly associated with the risk score, whereas ST2 (ng/mL) was not (44; 60; 45 p = 0.23). The IABP-SHOCK II risk score predicted 30-day mortality (score 0-2: 22%; score 4/3: 51%; score 5-9: 72%, area under the curve (AUC): 0.73, plogrank < 0.0001), while the tested biomarkers did not (AUC: 0.51<plogrank < 0.57). CONCLUSION: Plasma concentrations of Copeptin, MRproADM and proANP were associated with the IABP-SHOCK II risk score in STEMI patients admitted with CS. The risk score predicted 30-day mortality, with no improvement in prediction when concentrations of the assessed biomarkers were added.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Josiassen, Jakob","Frydland, Martin","Holmvang, Lene","Lerche Helgestad, Ole Kristian","Okkels Jensen, Lisette","Goetze, Jens P.","Eifer Møller, Jacob","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-099.93-042237"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Josiassen, Jakob"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Cardiogenic shock","Inflammation","Myocardial Infarction","Neurohormonal activation","STEMI"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mortality in cardiogenic shock is stronger associated to clinical factors than contemporary biomarkers reflecting neurohormonal stress and inflammatory activation","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85088310543","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by Rigshospitalets Forskningsfond [grant number: 07IO], Forskningspuljen ml. RH og OUH [grant number 13-A750, 25-A1365], The Danish Heart Foundation (Hjerteforeningen) [grant number A6024 and A8472], the J?rgen M?ller foundation and Hjertecentrets Forskningsudvalg, Rigshospitalet (no grant number). The authors would like to acknowledge the valuable contribution of the staff in the Catheterization Laboratory, the Coronary Care Unit, and the Intensive Care Unit at Odense University Hospital and Copenhagen University Hospital, Rigshospitalet."],"id":"S02-099.93-042237","identifier":[{"id":"32649233","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85088310543","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4ca40eba-b604-4fb7-83b3-377646739867","sdu-deab4f5d-495c-4214-84af-3a3657dca9c8"],"keyword":["Cardiogenic shock","IABP-SHOCK II risk score","STEMI","biomarkers","inflammation","myocardial infarction","neurohormonal activation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-478E0831D370A7B0FA0AADB79BAB31E0"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Mental Health Services Glostrup"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob","key":"josiassenpau","last":"Josiassen","name":"Josiassen, Jakob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"frydlandpau","last":"Frydland","name":"Frydland, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene","key":"holmvangpau","last":"Holmvang","locid":"54b8ef01-f8ed-4c49-a126-2109e2fd351f","name":"Holmvang, Lene","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole Kristian","key":"lerchehelgestadpau","last":"Lerche Helgestad","locid":"ab9f3165-500c-482b-9c2f-1879b3abedb3","name":"Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","name_org":"Lerche Helgestad, Ole Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-3847-8758","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette","key":"okkelsjensenpau","last":"Okkels Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","name_org":"Okkels Jensen, Lisette","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jens Peter","key":"goetzepau","last":"Goetze","locid":"980bceaf-dbf3-4f7a-a8d7-0a8e81b638b2","name":"Goetze, Jens P.","name_org":"Goetze, Jens Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-6356-3829","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"eifermøllerpau","last":"Eifer Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","name_org":"Eifer Møller, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32649233"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/1354750x.2020.1795265","issn":["1354750X","13665804"],"issn_org":["1354750X"],"issue":"6","journal":"Biomarkers","pages":"506-512","publisher":"Informa Healthcare","status":"p","title":"Biomarkers","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088310543"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4ca40eba-b604-4fb7-83b3-377646739867","sdu-deab4f5d-495c-4214-84af-3a3657dca9c8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Mortality in cardiogenic shock is stronger associated to clinical factors than contemporary biomarkers reflecting neurohormonal stress and inflammatory activation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.93-042237","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: To investigate the effect of the sodium-glucose co-transporter-2 inhibitor empagliflozin on N-terminal pro-b-type natriuretic peptide (NT-proBNP) in patients with heart failure (HF) and reduced ejection fraction (HFrEF). METHODS AND RESULTS: Empire HF was an investigator-initiated, multi-center, double-blinded, placebo-controlled, randomized trial. Patients with mildly symptomatic HFrEF, mean (standard deviation (SD)) age 64 (11) years, 85% male, and mean left ventricular ejection fraction 29% (8), on recommended HF therapy were assigned to receive either empagliflozin 10 mg once daily or placebo for 12 weeks. The primary endpoint was the between-group difference in the change of NT-proBNP from baseline to 12 weeks. In total, 95 patients were assigned to empagliflozin and 95 to placebo. No significant difference in the change of NT-proBNP with empagliflozin versus placebo was observed [Empagliflozin: baseline, median (interquartile range (IQR)) 582 (304-1020) pg/mL, 12 weeks, 478 (281-961) pg/mL; Placebo: baseline, 605 (322-1070) pg/mL, 12 weeks, 520 (267-1075) pg/mL, adjusted ratio of change empagliflozin/placebo 0.98; 95% confidence interval (CI) 0.82-1.11, P = 0.7]. Further, no significant difference was observed in accelerometer-measured daily activity level [adjusted mean difference of change, empagliflozin versus placebo, -26.0 accelerometer counts; 95% CI -88.0 to 36.0, P = 0.4] or Kansas City Cardiomyopathy Questionnaire Overall Summary Score [adjusted mean difference of change, empagliflozin versus placebo 0.8; 95% CI -2.3 to 3.9, P = 0.6]. CONCLUSION: In low-risk patients with HFrEF with mild symptoms and on recommended HF therapy, empagliflozin did not change NT-proBNP after 12 weeks. Further, no change in daily activity level or health status was observed.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Jensen, Jesper","Omar, Massar","Kistorp, Caroline","Poulsen, Mikael Kjær","Tuxen, Christian","Gustafsson, Ida","Køber, Lars","Gustafsson, Finn","Faber, Jens","Fosbøl, Emil L.","Bruun, Niels Eske","Brønd, Jan Christian","Forman, Julie Lyng","Videbæk, Lars","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Schou, Morten"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-010922"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Jesper"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"twelve weeks of treatment with empagliflozin in patients with heart failure and reduced ejection fraction a double blinded randomized and placebo controlled trial","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ahj.2020.07.011","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Research Council at Herlev and Gentofte University Hospital, Denmark [institutional research grant]; the Research and Innovation Foundation of the Department of Cardiology (FUHAS, formerly FUKAP), Herlev and Gentofte University Hospital, Denmark [institutional research grant]; the Capital Region of Denmark [grant number A6058]; the Danish Heart Foundation [grant numbers 17-R116-A7714-22076, 18-R124-A8573-22107]; the A.P. Møller Foundation for the Advancement of Medical Science [grant number 17-L-0002] and the Steno Diabetes Center Odense, Denmark [grant number 3363]. Dr Jensen reports grants from the Research Council at Herlev and Gentofte University Hospital, Denmark, grants from the Research and Innovation Foundation of the Department of Cardiology ((FUHAS, formerly FUKAP), Herlev and Gentofte University Hospital, Denmark, grants from the A.P. Møller Foundation for the Advancement of Medical Science, Denmark, during the conduct of the study. Dr Omar reports grants from The Steno Diabetes Center Odense, Denmark, during the conduct of the study. Dr Kistorp reports personal fees from scientific advisory panel and speaker fees from Boehringer Ingelheim, Merck, Sharp & Dohme, AstraZeneca, Amgen, Novartis, Novo Nordisk and Shire, outside the submitted work. Dr Poulsen has nothing to disclose. Dr Tuxen has nothing to disclose. Dr I. Gustafsson has nothing to disclose. Dr Køber reports personal fees from speaker honorarium from Novartis, AstraZeneca and Boehringer Ingelheim, outside the submitted work. Dr F. Gustafsson reports personal fees from Boehringer Ingelheim, during the conduct of the study; personal fees from Novartis, grants and personal fees from Pfizer, personal fees from Orion Pharma Abbott, Bayer, AstraZeneca and Carmat, outside the submitted work. Dr Faber has nothing to disclose. Dr Fosbøl has nothing to disclose. Dr Bruun has nothing to disclose. Dr Brønd has nothing to disclose. Dr Forman has nothing to disclose. Dr Videbæk has nothing to disclose. Dr Møller reports grants and personal fees from Abiomed, personal fees from Novartis and Orion Pharma, outside the submitted work. Dr Schou reports grants from The Capital Region of Denmark, grants from The Danish Heart Foundation, during the conduct of the study; personal fees and non-financial support from AstraZeneca, personal fees from Novo Nordisk and Boehringer Ingelheim, outside the submitted work."],"id":"S03-100.00-010922","identifier":[{"id":"85089349743","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32798787","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-e45ba291-dab4-443b-a836-2f6a09bccbdd","ku-3b2199f9-63f8-4987-9350-4d3b8336b185","sdu-2ca9cc55-c059-4033-928d-b91d1a990680"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-2D19BA22604BB43C0A04D4D1C2BEA8B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND 4.0","