","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Morten","key":"schoumortenpau","last":"Schou","locid":"48fa6ec9-1941-4566-b931-14b0cc8cbae3","name":"Schou, Morten","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32798787"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ahj.2020.07.011","issn":["00028703","10976744"],"issn_org":["00028703"],"journal":"American Heart Journal","pages":"47-56","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"American Heart Journal","volume":"228"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089349743"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e45ba291-dab4-443b-a836-2f6a09bccbdd","ku-3b2199f9-63f8-4987-9350-4d3b8336b185","sdu-2ca9cc55-c059-4033-928d-b91d1a990680"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Twelve weeks of treatment with empagliflozin in patients with heart failure and reduced ejection fraction : A double-blinded, randomized, and placebo-controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-010922","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background and aim This study aimed to assess right ventricular (RV) function during cardiogenic shock due to acute left ventricular (LV) failure, including during LV unloading with Impella CP and an added moderate dose of norepinephrine. Methods Cardiogenic shock was induced by injecting microspheres in the left main coronary artery in 18 adult Danish Landrace pigs. Conductance catheters were placed in both ventricles and pressure-volume loops were recorded simultaneously. Results Cardiogenic shock due to LV failure also impaired RV performance, which was partially restored during haemodynamic support with Impella CP, as demonstrated by changes in the ventriculo-arterial coupling (Ea/Ees ratio) (baseline (median [Q1;Q3]) 1.2 [1.1;1.6]), cardiogenic shock (3.0 [2.4;4.5]), Impella CP (2.1 [1.3;2.7]) (pBaseline vs CS < 0.0001, pCS vs Impella = 0.001)). Impella CP support also improved RV stroke work (SW) (cardiogenic shock 333 [263;530] vs Impella CP (830 [717;1121]) (p < 0.001). Moderate norepinephrine infusion concomitant with Impella CP further improved RV SW (Impella CP (818 [751;1065]) vs Impella CP+moderate norepinephrine (1231 [1142;1335]) (p = 0.01)) but at the expense of an increase in LV SW (Impella CP (858 [555;1392]) vs Impella CP+moderate norepinephrine (2101 [1024;2613]) (p = 0.04)). Conclusions The Impella CP provided efficient LV unloading, improved RV function, and end-organ perfusion. Moderate doses of norepinephrine during Impella support further improved RV function, but at the expense of an increase in SW of the failing LV.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Josiassen, Jakob","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Udesen, Nanne Louise Junker","Banke, Ann","Frederiksen, Peter Hartmund","Hyldebrandt, Janus Adler","Schmidt, Henrik","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Hassager, Christian","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Moller, Jacob E."],"cuid":["S02-099.69-044214"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Josiassen, Jakob"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["Akershus University Hospital","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Acute heart failure","Cardiogenic shock","Left ventricular assist device","Mechanical circulatory support","Vasopressor therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unloading using impella cp during profound cardiogenic shock caused by left ventricular failure in a large animal model impact on the right ventricle","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40635-020-00326-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.69-044214","identifier":[{"id":"32785808","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000559895500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC7423825","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85105492876","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8b0dcf35-69da-49a0-995b-cdc6f5e20783","sdu-8859b9de-a6d7-43d2-9ccb-7055639e60ac"],"keyword":["Acute heart failure","Cardiogenic shock","Left ventricular assist device","Mechanical circulatory support","Vasopressor therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2367391BBA0CAB75BCD0F2EDE5F55034"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250554324/s40635_020_00326_y.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/179223658/s40635_020_00326_y.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40635-020-00326-y","version":"Published Version"}],"oa