5608","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Cardiogenic shock (CS) due to myocardial infarction (MI) carries 30-day mortality rates as high as 50\\of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA). Patients with and without OHCA are likely to represent two distinctive entities, which may be problematic to combine in an intervention trial.The aim of the study was to compare CS due to MI patients presenting with and without OHCA in terms of patient characteristics and outcome.In the period from 2010–2017 all patients admitted at two tertiary heart centres in Denmark with CS following MI were individually identified and validated through patient records. The two centres have a catchment area of 3.9 million citizens corresponding to two-thirds of the Danish population.A total of 1716 CS patients were identified, of which 42\\mean 63 vs 67 years), more frequently male (85 vs 67\\, had higher lactate concentration (median 6.2 vs 5.0 mmol/L) on admission and higher left ventricular ejection fraction (median 30 vs 25\\ compared to patients without OHCA (p\\lt;0.0001 for all). Patients presenting with OHCA had lower 30-day mortality compared to patients without OHCA (49\\7\\ respectively, plogrank\\lt;0.0001, Figure). Cause of in hospital death differed markedly between the two groups. Not surprisingly, anoxic brain damage was the leading cause of in hospital death in the OHCA group (56\\ and only seen in 4\\ cardiac failure was the main cause of death in hospital death among patients without OHCA (60\\, compared to 27\\p\\lt;0.0001).Figure 1Among patients with CS due to MI, overall 30-day mortality was significantly lower in patients presenting with OHCA. Anoxic brain damage was the main cause of in hospital death among OHCA patients, whereas fatal heart failure prevailed in patients without OHCA. Combining these two groups in a single trial with one specific intervention seems inappropriate and likely to cause an imbalance in the signal-to-noise ratio.The Danish Heart Foundation and a research grant from Abiomed","author_count":9,"contributors":["Josiassen, J","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Kjaergaard, J","Schmidt, Henrik","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Holmvang, L","Ravn, H B","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-614034"],"event":{"end":"2019-09-04","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2019-08-31","title":"European Society of Cardiology congress 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cardiogenic shock patients those with and those without out of hospital cardiac arrest are different clinical entities","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-614034","ids":["sdu-8e73fd24-a062-4343-8699-5805a4f14bc3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-779FF6B07AD6C40522DBB8B71ADD20F0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J","key":"josiassenpau","last":"Josiassen","name":"Josiassen, J","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"O K L","key":"helgestadpau","last":"Helgestad","locid":"ab9f3165-500c-482b-9c2f-1879b3abedb3","name":"Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","name_org":"Helgestad, O K L","orcid":"0000-0003-3847-8758","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J E","key":"moellerpau","last":"Moeller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","name_org":"Moeller, J E","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","name":"Kjaergaard, J","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"H","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","name_org":"Schmidt, H","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"L O","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","name_org":"Jensen, L O","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L","key":"holmvangpau","last":"Holmvang","name":"Holmvang, L","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"H B","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","name":"Ravn, H B","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"C","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"4025bf39-1de8-49eb-975c-cbc1a5f906ff","name":"Hassager, Christian","name_org":"Hassager, C","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/eurheartj/ehz748.0483","issn":["0195668X","15229645"],"issn_org":["0195668X"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"European Heart Journal","pages":"1026","paperid":"ehz748.0483","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal","volume":"40"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8e73fd24-a062-4343-8699-5805a4f14bc3"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Cardiogenic shock patients: those with and those without out-of-hospital cardiac arrest are different clinical entities","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-614034","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: The diagnosis of cardiogenic shock depends on clinical signs of poor perfusion and low blood pressure. Lactate concentration will increase with poor tissue perfusion, and it has prognostic value in cardiogenic shock patients. We sought to assess the prognostic value of lactate concentration in subjects admitted with suspected ST-elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI). METHODS AND RESULTS: In 2,094 (93%) out of 2,247 consecutive suspected STEMI-subjects, lactate concentration was measured on admission. The prognostic value of lactate concentration on 30-day mortality was assessed in addition to clinical signs of peripheral hypoperfusion, systolic blood pressure (sBP), and left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) in multivariable models.Lactate concentration added prognostic information beyond signs of peripheral hypoperfusion, sBP, and LVEF, and was independently associated with 30-day mortality (hazard ratio [95% confidence interval] 1.11 [1.07-1.14], P < 0.0001). Lactate also provided predictive information on 30-day mortality to the combination of signs of peripheral hypoperfusion, sBP, and LVEF (area under the receiver-operating characteristics curve = 0.88 vs. 0.83, P < 0.0001). CONCLUSIONS: In conclusion, admission lactate concentration in suspected STEMI-subjects contains prognostic information on 30-day mortality when added to variables used in cardiogenic shock-definition. We recommend lactate measurement in STEMI-subjects, especially when signs of compromised hemodynamics are present.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Frydland, Martin","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Wiberg, Sebastian","Lindholm, Matias Greve","Hansen, Rikke","Henriques, Jose P S","Møller-Helgestad, Ole Kristian","Bang, Lia Evi","Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth","Goetze, Jens Peter","Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","Thomsen, Jakob Hartvig","Ouweneel, Dagmar M","Obling, Laust","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Holmvang, Lene","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S0