"3049e7b7-0f18-413b-88ab-a3d77ebc079b","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","name_org":"Ravn, Hanne B.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob E","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","name_org":"Møller, Jacob E","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31339222"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ejhf.1566","issn":["13889842","18790844"],"issn_org":["13889842"],"issue":"11","journal":"European Journal of Heart Failure","pages":"1370-1378","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Heart Failure","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85069705846"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bd0a5d96-950b-4f27-9466-c0dc4b37bd26","sdu-7e701fcc-1b42-4e40-8f4b-1da24e93276c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Temporal trends in incidence and patient characteristics in cardiogenic shock following acute myocardial infarction from 2010 to 2017 : a Danish cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-045776","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Data from recent cardiovascular outcome trials in patients with type 2 diabetes (T2D) suggest that sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitors can prevent development of heart failure (HF) and prolong life in patients without HF. Ongoing event-driven trials are investigating whether the same effect is present in patients with well-defined HF. The mechanism behind the effect of SGLT2 inhibitors in patients with T2D and the potential effect in patients with overt HF is presently unknown. METHODS: This is a randomized, double-blinded, placebo-controlled, parallel group, clinical trial including HF patients with reduced left ventricular ejection fraction (HFrEF) with an ejection fraction ≤ 40% on optimal therapy recruited from specialized HF clinics in Denmark. The primary aim is to investigate the effect of the SGLT2 inhibitor empagliflozin on N-terminal pro-brain natriuretic peptide (NT-proBNP). Secondary endpoints include cardiac biomarkers, function and hemodynamics, metabolic and renal parameters, daily activity level, and quality of life. Patients are assigned 1:1 to 90 days treatment with empagliflozin 10 mg daily or placebo. Patients with T2D are required to be on recommended doses of anti-glycemic therapy with a hemoglobin A1c (HbA1c) of 6.5-10.0% (48-86 mmol/mol). To show a between-group difference in the change of NT-proBNP of 30%, a total of 189 patients will be included. DISCUSSION: The Empire HF trial will elucidate the effects and modes of action of empagliflozin in HFrEF patients with and without T2D and provide important mechanistic data which will complement ongoing event-driven trials. TRIAL REGISTRATION: Clinicaltrialsregister.eu, EudraCT Number 2017-001341-27 . Registered on 29 May 2017. ClinicalTrials.gov, NCT03198585 . Registered on 26 June 2017.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Jensen, Jesper","Omar, Massar","Kistorp, Caroline","Poulsen, Mikael Kjær","Tuxen, Christian","Gustafsson, Ida","Køber, Lars","Gustafsson, Finn","Fosbøl, Emil","Bruun, Niels Eske","Videbæk, Lars","Frederiksen, Peter Hartmund","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Schou, Morten"],"cuid":["S03-099.97-010581"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Jesper"],"keyword":["Benzhydryl Compounds adverse effects","Cardiac function","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 complications","Double Blind Method","Glucosides adverse effects","Heart Failure drug therapy","Heart failure","Humans","Mechanism","Mode of action","NT proBNP","Natriuretic Peptide Brain blood","Peptide Fragments blood","Quality of Life","Renal endpoints","SGLT2 inhibitors","Sodium Glucose Transporter 2 Inhibitors therapeutic use","Stroke Volume drug effects"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Copenhagen University, Blegdamsvej 3B, 2200, København N, DK, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"empagliflozin in heart failure patients with reduced ejection fraction a randomized clinical trial empire hf","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-019-3474-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.97-010581","identifier":[{"id":"85068511791","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31227014","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6588901","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-de0f2019-7a52-4a49-918d-068461251bee","ku-0941a1f6-6472-44ac-95bd-fb894c73d214","sdu-8765a7fb-684b-4b32-9faa-d19e591d3adb"],"keyword":["Benzhydryl Compounds/adverse effects","Cardiac function","Daily activity level","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/complications","Double-Blind Method","Glucosides/adverse effects","Heart Failure/drug therapy","Heart failure","Humans","Mechanism","Metabolic endpoints","Mode of action","NT-proBNP","Natriuretic Peptide, Brain/blood","Peptide Fragments/blood","Quality of Life","Renal endpoints","SGLT2 inhibitors","Sodium-Glucose Transporter 2 Inhibitors/therapeutic use","Stroke Volume/drug effects"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-02E49DD6810E929E24580B0EE80741BB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/152258060/Empagliflozin_in_heart_failure_patients_with_reduced_ejection_fraction.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/307378825/Jensen_et_al._2019_Empagliflozin_in_heart_failure_patients_with_reduced_ejection_fraction.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-019-3474-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/236220601/document_10_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU