:"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frank Møller","key":"aarestruppau","last":"Aarestrup","locid":"8a1eb030-2c37-4557-bce1-7bc6d5c75aaa","name":"Aarestrup, Frank Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-7116-2723","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"hasmanpau","last":"Hasman","locid":"2aeb80b4-d42a-4da2-9212-86b697184f40","name":"Hasman, Henrik","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25428145"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/jcm.03104-14","issn":["00951137","1070633X"],"issn_org":["00951137"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Clinical Microbiology","pages":"677-680","publisher":"American Society for Microbiology","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Microbiology","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84921783012"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-15adf70a-1f48-4559-8091-e1fde89b456e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Genomic Dissection of Travel-Associated Extended-Spectrum-Beta-Lactamase-Producing Salmonella enterica Serovar Typhi Isolates Originating from the Philippines: a One-Off Occurrence or a Threat to Effective Treatment of Typhoid Fever?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-311109","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Retrospectively, we investigated the epidemiology of a massive Salmonella enterica serovar Typhi outbreak in Zambia during 2010 to 2012. Ninety-four isolates were susceptibility tested by MIC determinations. Whole-genome sequence typing (WGST) of 33 isolates and bioinformatic analysis identified the multilocus sequence type (MLST), haplotype, plasmid replicon, antimicrobial resistance genes, and genetic relatedness by single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) analysis and genomic deletions. The outbreak affected 2,040 patients, with a fatality rate of 0.5%. Most (83.0%) isolates were multidrug resistant (MDR). The isolates belonged to MLST ST1 and a new variant of the haplotype, H58B. Most isolates contained a chromosomally translocated region containing seven antimicrobial resistance genes, catA1, blaTEM-1, dfrA7, sul1, sul2, strA, and strB, and fragments of the incompatibility group Q1 (IncQ1) plasmid replicon, the class 1 integron, and the mer operon. The genomic analysis revealed 415 SNP differences overall and 35 deletions among 33 of the isolates subjected to whole-genome sequencing. In comparison with other genomes of H58, the Zambian isolates separated from genomes from Central Africa and India by 34 and 52 SNPs, respectively. The phylogenetic analysis indicates that 32 of the 33 isolates sequenced belonged to a tight clonal group distinct from other H58 genomes included in the study. The small numbers of SNPs identified within this group are consistent with the short-term transmission that can be expected over a period of 2 years. The phylogenetic analysis and deletions suggest that a single MDR clone was responsible for the outbreak, during which occasional other S. Typhi lineages, including sensitive ones, continued to cocirculate. The common view is that the emerging global S. Typhi haplotype, H58B, containing the MDR IncHI1 plasmid is responsible for the majority of typhoid infections in Asia and sub-Saharan Africa; we found that a new variant of the haplotype harboring a chromosomally translocated region containing the MDR islands of IncHI1 plasmid has emerged in Zambia. This could change the perception of the term \"classical MDR typhoid\" currently being solely associated with the IncHI1 plasmid. It might be more common than presently thought that S. Typhi haplotype H58B harbors the IncHI1 plasmid or a chromosomally translocated MDR region or both.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Hendriksen, Rene S.","Leekitcharoenphon, Pimlapas","Lukjancenko, Oksana","Lukwesa-Musyani, Chileshe","Tambatamba, Bushimbwa","Mwaba, John","Kalonda, Annie","Nakazwe, Ruth","Kwenda, Geoffrey","Jensen, Jacob Dyring","Svendsen, Christina Aaby","Dittmann, Karen Kiesbye","Kaas, Rolf Sommer","Cavaco, Lina","Aarestrup, Frank Møller","Hasman, Henrik","Mwansa, James C. L."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-372797"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Zambia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ministry of Health Zambia","University Teaching Hospital Lusaka","University of Zambia"],"keyword":["Bacteriology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genomic signature of multidrug resistant salmonella enterica serovar typhi isolates related to a massive outbreak in zambia between 000000002010 and 000000002012","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/JCM.02026-14","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-372797","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4290967","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84919477769","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25392358","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-e4454715-e6db-4151-b19a-00c67b81167a"],"keyword":["Bacteriology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-28A4C040152CBFE98B302237E6020082"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/JCM.02026-14","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Division of Epidemiology and Microbial Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"zm","key":"university teaching hospital lusaka","loc":["Zambia","Africa"],"name":"University Teaching Hospital Lusaka","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"zm","key":"ministry of health zambia","loc":["Zambia","Africa"],"name":"Ministry of Health Zambia","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"zm","key":"university of zambia","loc":["Zambia","Africa"],"name":"University of Zambia","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rene S.","key":"hendriksenpau","last":"Hendriksen","locid":"d0695f89-50d1-4626-b4b2-0ea8773ccb3c","name":"Hendriksen, Rene S.","orcid":"0000-0003-2934-8214","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pimlapas","key":"leekitcharoenphonpau","last":"Leekitcharoenphon","locid":"432b3315-1807-49ee-a83f-d4ea2a9219d1","name":"Leekitcharoenphon, Pimlapas","orcid":"0000-0002-5674-0142","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oksana","key":"lukjancenkopau","last":"Lukjancenko","locid":"21a7ee27-6d90-489b-b8be-207b1e8e7b28","name":"Lukjancenko, Oksana","orcid":"0000-0003-0102-0364","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Chileshe","key":"lukwesamusy