"name":"Richter, Erik A.","orcid":"0000-0002-6850-3056","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23671593"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0062338","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"5","journal":"PLOS ONE","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84877089184"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-41f014cb-a379-4682-b890-af29dc483793"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"AMPK and insulin action : Responses to ageing and high fat diet","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-432857","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"A Danish municipality has introduced a 2-compartment bin in the waste collection scheme, this bin should increase recycling of dry household recyclables. An excessive waste sorting campaign was conducted and the efficiency of the bin assessed. The waste sorting campaign yielded a full waste composition with focus on the dry recyclables, and it was used to determine wheter the 2-compartment bin could fulfill the EU recycling targets for 2020. Only 2 of 4 calculation methods for meeting the EU targets were applicable and only one of these fulfilled the EU target. Eventhough the EU recycling targets can be fulfilled, there is still room for improvement (increase source separation), especially for hard plastic and metals.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Morten Bang","Scheutz, Charlotte","Møller, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352922"],"event":{"end":"2013-10-04","place":"Cagliari, it","start":"2013-09-30","title":"Sardinia 2013 - 14th International Waste Management and Landfill Symposium","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"meeting the eu recycling targets by introducing a 000000000002 compartment bin to households","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-352922","ids":["dtu-a21174cd-8bdd-4b45-94c0-e8ae5083b802"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-87C04475F753CDAAA77806F701F52032"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering, Residual Resource Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Bang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"647f1ac7-93b2-4476-9ff2-a2d1a245e948","name":"Jensen, Morten Bang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"scheutzpau","last":"Scheutz","locid":"48fe2850-fdc6-4282-9b97-ac5773419e5c","name":"Scheutz, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-2218-5934","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"ba375b02-d34a-4a26-958d-59b8bd17fa42","name":"Møller, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0003-3475-1251","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["11. Sustainable Cities and Production","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a21174cd-8bdd-4b45-94c0-e8ae5083b802"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Meeting the EU recycling targets by introducing a 2-compartment bin to households","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352922","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The majority of patients with end stage renal disease are in hemodialysis, and therefore dependent on a well functioning vascular access. The arteriovenous fistula is the recommended access and in order to maintain and keep the fistula patent, regular monitoring of the function is necessary. The Ultrasound Dilution Technique is the reference method for volume flow measurement, but it only works in conjunction with the dialysis machine, and use is therefore restricted to dialysis sessions. Volume flow measurement with conventional Doppler ultrasound provides a non invasive, highly accessible solution, but is very challenging due to the angle dependency of the Doppler technique and the anatomy of the fistula. The angle independent vector ultrasound technique Transverse Oscillation provides a new and more intuitive way to measure volume flow in an arteriovenous fistula. In this paper the Transverse Oscillation has been used to measure volume flow directly on four patients’ arteriovenous fistulas, and the measurements were compared to subsequent measurements with the Ultrasound Dilution Technique. The results obtained with the Transverse Oscillation deviate -35.1 – 14.9 % from the reference method, and indicates potential for the method.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hansen, Peter Møller","Heerwagen, Søren","Pedersen, Mads Møller","Rix, Marianne","Lönn, Lars","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Olesen, Jacob Bjerring","Pihl, Michael Johannes","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-379363"],"event":{"end":"2013-07-25","place":"Prague, cz","start":"2013-07-21","title":"2013 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Arteriovenous fistula","Doppler","Transverse oscillation","Volume flow"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vector volume flow in arteriovenous fistulas","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/57407856/vector_volume_flow.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-379363","identifier":[{"id":"84894318518","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f9f0604d-1f90-4094-b16d-9ae4e28a28cc"],"keyword":["Arteriovenous fistula","Doppler","Transverse oscillation","Ultrasound dilution","Vector ultrasound","Volume flow"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A39BE8571F5FD034D0467749EBF3EE48"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/57407856/vector_volume_flow.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Fast Ultrasound Imaging","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Møller","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3fd47ccb-1081-429f-8844-