{"abstract":"Consumer nickel sensitization and dermatitis is caused by prolonged or repeated skin exposure to items that release nickel, for example jewellery, belts, buttons, watches, and mobile phones (1–3). We recently described a patient in whom primary nickel contact sensitization and dermatitis developed following the use of an Apple laptop computer (4). To estimate nickel release from Apple laptop computers, we investigated a random sample of 20 devices.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jensen, Peter","Jellesen, Morten Stendahl","Møller, Per","Johansen, Jeanne Duus","Liden, Carola","Menne, Torkil","Thyssen, Jacob Pontoppidan"],"cuid":["S02-092.46-035528"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institutet"],"keyword":["Consumer","Dermatitis","Nickel"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Materials Science and Engineering"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nickel may be released from laptop computers","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-0536.2012.02162.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-092.46-035528","identifier":[{"id":"84869465565","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23151198","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-7fc5d976-d0f1-44ce-9bb3-bfc50d4efd6f","ku-347b93cf-de10-46c8-802e-cb9e631a2bee"],"keyword":["Consumer","Dermatitis","Nickel"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-017D0EB6AEA3A06870BFF3F3B7A0CD73"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url