79-02be-4043-8f66-88b1b123c60f","ku-8a4990a8-9a85-4f4e-848f-888a064a2458","nfa-5d72fd68-280e-431a-9ba9-85dd71563e1f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Oxidative Stress, DNA Damage, and Inflammation Induced by Ambient Air and Wood Smoke Particulate Matter in Human A549 and THP-1 Cell Lines","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-095.93-767208","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"A number of methods for ultrasound vector velocity imaging are presented in the paper. The transverse oscillation (TO) method can estimate the velocity transverse to the ultrasound beam by introducing a lateral oscillation in the received ultrasound field. The approach has been thoroughly investigated using both simulations, flow rig measurements, and in-vivo validation against MR scans. The TO method obtains a relative accuracy of 10% for a fully transverse flow in both simulations and flow rig experiments. In-vivo studies performed on 11 healthy volunteers comparing the TO method with magnetic resonance phase contrast angiography (MRA) revealed a correlation between the stroke volume estimated by TO and MRA of 0.91 (p<;0.01) with an equation for the line of regression given as: MRA = 1.1 · TO-0.4 ml. Several clinical examples of complex flow in e.g. bifurcations and around valves have been acquired using a commercial implementation of the method (BK Medical ProFocus Ultraview scanner). A range of other methods are also presented. This includes synthetic aperture imaging using either spherical or plane waves with velocity estimation performed with directional beamforming or speckle tracking. The key advantages of these techniques are very fast imaging that can attain an order of magnitude higher precision than conventional methods. SA flow imaging was implemented on the experimental scanner RASMUS using an 8-emission spherical emission sequence and reception of 64 channels on a BK Medical 8804 transducer. This resulted in a relative standard deviation of 1.2% for a fully transverse flow. Plane wave imaging was also implemented on the RASMUS scanner and a 100 Hz frame rate was attained. Several vector velocity image sequences of complex flow were acquired, which demonstrates the benefits of fast vector flow imaging. A method for extending the 2D TO method to 3D vector velocity estimation is presented and the implications for future vector velocity imagi- g is indicated.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","Nikolov, Svetoslav","Udesen, Jesper","Munk, Peter","Hansen, Kristoffer Lindskov","Pedersen, Mads Møller","Hansen, Peter Møller","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Oddershede, Niels","Kortbek, Jacob","Pihl, Michael Johannes","Li, Ye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-365312"],"event":{"end":"2011-10-21","place":"Orlando, us","start":"2011-10-18","title":"2011 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Apertures","Estimation","Image color analysis","Imaging","Oscillators","Ultrasonic imaging","Vectors"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"recent advances in blood flow vector velocity imaging","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5865570/preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-365312","identifier":[{"id":"84869022028","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cb698814-1279-4ee5-adbd-f686e222cad0"],"keyword":["Apertures","Estimation","Image color analysis","Imaging","Oscillators","Ultrasonic imaging","Vectors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B3D956EC2902B659D888B5BB32E2FA64"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ewh.ieee.org/conf/ius_2011/index.html","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ULTSYM.2011.0064","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5865570/preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Fast Ultrasound Imaging","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["BK Medical ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenjørgenarendtpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Svetoslav","key":"nikolovsvetoslavpau","last":"Nikolov","locid":"4009cc9a-9642-4c22-b453-8de1f17baf12","name":"Nikolov, Svetoslav","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"udesenjesperpau","last":"Udesen","locid":"7a1a9328-2acb-45ee-9e91-332a22e1f4a0","name":"Udesen, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"munkpeterpau","last":"Munk","locid":"82ed3f76-4387-459c-8954-d0bcc3